{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01URyn3ZBqg8ZKXS45q8o2TL","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tnarrative_guidance: 'Cheetah 未能干净复现 CIVO 模式（NVE 停留在 0.8-1.4x，无加速性过估计签名），Cartpole/ManiSkill3\n2\t  亦无清晰 CIVO 信号。 论文退守为 Walker Walk 单环境深度机制研究。核心贡献重新定位为： (1) 首个严格析因诊断——在 DreamerV3 imagination-based\n3\t  actor-critic 中揭示 temporal abstraction 失败的 specific causal chain； (2) NVE 诊断方法论（Walker\n4\t  内 4/4 完美分类，提议更广泛使用但承认跨环境泛化受限）； (3) gradient-level 因果证据（Full-SGS NVE 1.00x）证明失败是\n5\t  observation-decoder-driven 而非 reward-driven——即便限于单环境亦非显然。 TAWM 对比成为 novelty 支柱：\"dt-conditioning\n6\t  在 MPC 中成功（TAWM, ICML 2025）但在 imagination 中失败——我们提供首个机制解释。\" 跨环境泛化声明全部删除，替换为 extensive\n7\t  limitations section 讨论 Cheetah/Cartpole 为何动力学不同 （reward density、state dimensionality、RSSM\n8\t  fidelity characteristics）。 仍可投 CoRL 作为 methodology + single-environment depth 论文，但接收概率下降；需\n9\t  exceptional writing quality 和 TAWM contrast 支撑 novelty。\n10\t\n11\t  '\n12\timagined_experiments:\n13\t- name: Walker Walk 008d (trained dt_emb, collapse) seeds 1-2\n14\t  plan_id: plan_011\n15\t  description: 复现 CIVO collapse，2 additional seeds\n16\t  expected_results:\n17\t    seed1_009e_final_eval: 131.08\n18\t    seed1_009e_peak_nve: 4.12\n19\t    seed1_009e_collapse: true\n20\t    seed2_009b_final_eval: 267.93\n21\t    seed2_009b_peak_nve: 2.05\n22\t    seed2_009b_collapse: false\n23\t    collapse_rate: 1/2 (50%)\n24\t    nve_gt_1_5x_rate: 2/2 (100%)\n25\t  result_rationale: '实际数据已收集。worst-tier 解读：collapse rate 仅 50%（1/2 独立 seed 崩溃）， 削弱\n26\t    \"CIVO 是 deterministic failure\" 的叙事。009b 的自修正（NVE 2.05x@25K → 0.38x@105K） 证明 CIVO\n27\t    反馈环并非不可逆——早期训练随机性决定路径分叉。这迫使论文用语从 \"trained dt_emb causes collapse\" 改为 \"trained\n28\t    dt_emb reliably triggers pathological overestimation (NVE>1.5x), with collapse\n29\t    as a stochastic consequence\"。 当 Cheetah 无法复现该模式时，50% collapse rate 的统计力量进一步被质疑。\n30\t\n31\t    '\n32\t  tables:\n33\t  - title: 008d config cross-seed comparison\n34\t    headers:\n35\t    - Metric\n36\t    - Seed 0 (008d)\n37\t    - Seed 1 (009e)\n38\t    - Seed 2 (009b)\n39\t    rows:\n40\t    - - Peak NVE (35K+)\n41\t      - 2.09x@45K\n42\t      - 4.12x@55K\n43\t      - 1.62x@45K\n44\t    - - Collapse?\n45\t      - Yes@55K\n46\t      - Yes@55K\n47\t      - No (self-correct)\n48\t    - - Final eval@105K\n49\t      - 82.7 (55K stop)\n50\t      - '131.1'\n51\t      - '267.9'\n52\t    - - NVE trajectory\n53\t      - accelerating\n54\t      - accelerating\n55\t      - transient peak → decline\n56\t  figures_description:\n57\t  - NVE 轨迹对比图：seed 0/1 加速发散 vs seed 2 自修正。标注 1.5x threshold 和 35K cutoff\n58\t  analysis: 'Walker 内 NVE>1.5x diagnostic 仍有 2/2 sensitivity（trained seeds 全部 exceed），\n59\t    但 collapse 的 stochastic nature 限制了 practical significance。当 Cheetah 数据加入 后（0/3\n60\t    exceed 1.5x），threshold 的跨环境推广将失败。Worst-tier 下这组数据 退化为 Walker-specific 机制证据而非 general\n61\t    vulnerability 证据。\n62\t\n63\t    '\n64\t- name: Walker Walk 008f (dt_embed_dim=0) seeds 1-2\n65\t  plan_id: plan_012\n66\t  description: 复现因果控制稳定性，2 additional seeds\n67\t  expected_results:\n68\t    seed1_009f_status: killed (incomplete)\n69\t    seed2_009c_final_eval: 148.34\n70\t    seed2_009c_peak_nve: 1.26\n71\t    seed2_009c_trend: peak 359@75K → decline to 148@105K\n72\t    seed2_009c_collapse: false\n73\t    protection_robust: false\n74\t  result_rationale: '实际数据：009f 被 kill（无完整数据），009c 在 75K 后持续下降至 148（vs baseline 916，仅\n75\t    16%）。 虽然 009c 的 NVE 始终 <1.5x（peak 1.26x@25K），符合 \"no CIVO\" 判定，但绝对性能极差。 Worst-tier\n76\t    解读：dt_embed_dim=0 的 \"保护\" 极不 robust——seed 0 恢复到 503 而 seed 2 跌至 148。 保护机制是 seed-dependent\n77\t    的，008f 不是可靠方案。因果方向（trained dt_emb → CIVO）仍成立 （两个 seed 均 NVE<1.5x），但 practical\n78\t    value 有限。\n79\t\n80\t    '\n81\t  tables:\n82\t  - title: 008f config cross-seed\n83\t    headers:\n84\t    - Metric\n85\t    - Seed 0 (008f)\n86\t    - Seed 2 (009c)\n87\t    rows:\n88\t    - - Peak NVE\n89\t      - 1.02x@25K\n90\t      - 1.26x@25K\n91\t    - - Final eval@105K\n92\t      - '503'\n93\t      - '148'\n94\t    - - Recovery pattern\n95\t      - Zigzag → 503\n96\t      - Peak 359@75K → decline\n97\t    - - vs baseline\n98\t      - -45%\n99\t      - -84%\n100\t  figures_description: []\n101\t  analysis: '009c 的衰退说明去掉 dt_embedding 虽阻止 CIVO 但不保证学习成功——reward prediction 退化（MAE\n102\t    75x baseline）本身就是严重代价。Worst-tier 下，这组数据用于因果论证 但不支持任何 practical recommendation。\n103\t\n104\t    '\n105\t- name: Walker Walk 008e_v3 (dt=1 imag) seeds 1-2\n106\t  plan_id: plan_014\n107\t  description: C6 mitigation multi-seed validation\n108\t  expected_results:\n109\t    seed1_eval_105K: 869.9\n110\t    seed1_nve_105K: 0.8\n111\t    seed1_collapse: false\n112\t    seed2_eval_105K: 137.0\n113\t    seed2_nve_105K: 3.78\n114\t    seed2_collapse: true\n115\t    seed2_collapse_mechanism: non-CIVO (eval-driven, entropy ↑)\n116\t    collapse_rate: 1/2 (50%)\n117\t    c6_status: PARTIALLY FALSIFIED\n118\t  result_rationale: '实际数据。s1 成功（95% baseline），s2 在 85-105K 崩溃（715→452→137），但机制与 经典\n119\t    CIVO 不同：s2 是 eval-driven（eval 先跌，value 稳定，entropy ↑），而 008d 是 value-driven（value\n120\t    爆炸，eval 后跌，entropy ↓）。009a baseline s2 在同期完全稳定 （618→596→836），排除 seed 脆弱性。Worst-tier\n121\t    解读：dt=1 imagination 未降低 collapse rate（与 dt=2 同为 50%），C6 mitigation 被 falsify。Trained\n122\t    dt_embedding 通过 Pathway B（non-CIVO policy instability）绕过 dt=1 保护。\n123\t\n124\t    '\n125\t  tables:\n126\t  - title: 008e_v3 Pathway A vs Pathway B\n127\t    headers:\n128\t    - Feature\n129\t    - '008d s0 (Pathway A: CIVO)'\n130\t    - '008e_v3 s2 (Pathway B: non-CIVO)'\n131\t    rows:\n132\t    - - Value change\n133\t      - +130% explosion\n134\t      - +13% stable\n135\t    - - Eval change\n136\t      - 后跌 -43%\n137\t      - 先跌 -81%\n138\t    - - NVE driver\n139\t      - Value 分子驱动\n140\t      - Eval 分母驱动\n141\t    - - Actor entropy\n142\t      - ↓ (-3.47→-4.88)\n143\t      - ↑ (-5.21→-3.83)\n144\t    - - Mechanism\n145\t      - Critic overestimate → actor exploit\n146\t      - Eval crash → value lag\n147\t  figures_description:\n148\t  - 双 pathway 对比图：value/eval/entropy 三轨并列，008d s0 vs 008e_v3 s2\n149\t  analysis: 'C6 partially falsified 是 worst-tier 最关键的负面结果。论文需重新定位 trained dt_embedding\n150\t    为 \"multi-pathway vulnerability creator\"，而非仅 CIVO trigger。但 Pathway B 机制 尚不充分理解——如果\n151\t    plan_016 显示仅 1/4 崩溃，Pathway B 可能退化为 seed variance。\n152\t\n153\t    '\n154\t- name: Walker Walk FROZEN dt_emb + subsample ON + dt=2 imag\n155\t  plan_id: plan_015\n156\t  description: 诊断 dt_emb TRAINING 是否为 CIVO 必要条件\n157\t  expected_results:\n158\t    final_eval_105K: 204.2\n159\t    nve_range: 0.39-0.47\n160\t    collapse: false\n161\t    collapse_mechanism: gradient starvation (actor_loss→0)\n162\t    gate_dt_mean: 2.0\n163\t    actor_loss_105K: 0.000179\n164\t  result_rationale: '实际数据（exp_015b）。Frozen dt_emb 导致 gradient starvation：随机初始化的 dt_embedding\n165\t    不训练，为 RSSM 提供无信息 conditioning→critic 系统性低估（NVE 0.39-0.47x）， actor loss 趋近零，学习停滞。eval\n166\t    在 80-238 间剧烈波动，无稳定收敛。 Worst-tier 解读：确认了一个消融点（frozen ≠ trained ≠ absent），但引入新失败模式\n167\t    （gradient starvation），不能作为 mitigation。论文仅能作为 mechanism isolation 证据： dt_emb 的\n168\t    training 过程本身驱动 CIVO。\n169\t\n170\t    '\n171\t  tables: []\n172\t  figures_description: []\n173\t  analysis: 'Frozen dt_emb 的 gradient starvation 是 worst-tier 下的一个 \"ugly control\"——\n174\t    它证明了 dt_emb training 是 CIVO 必要条件，但方式不够 clean（引入新问题而非 neutral baseline）。论文中需小心呈现：这是析因矩阵中的一个消融点，而非独立\n175\t    finding。\n176\t\n177\t    '\n178\t- name: Walker Walk 008a (untrained dt_emb, V-recovery) seeds 1-2\n179\t  plan_id: plan_013\n180\t  description: 复现 value growth suppression，2 additional seeds\n181\t  expected_results:\n182\t    seed1_eval_trajectory:\n183\t      35K: 460\n184\t      45K: 510\n185\t      55K: 440\n186\t      65K: 550\n187\t      75K: 480\n188\t      85K: 530\n189\t      95K: 520\n190\t      105K: 700\n191\t    seed1_nve_range_55K_105K:\n192\t    - 0.6\n193\t    - 0.85\n194\t    seed1_final_eval: 700\n195\t    seed1_vs_baseline_105K: -23.5%\n196\t    seed2_eval_trajectory:\n197\t      35K: 420\n198\t      45K: 480\n199\t      55K: 400\n200\t      65K: 470\n201\t      75K: 430\n202\t      85K: 510\n203\t      95K: 490\n204\t      105K: 620\n205\t    seed2_nve_range_55K_105K:\n206\t    - 0.55\n207\t    - 0.8\n208\t    seed2_final_eval: 620\n209\t    seed2_vs_baseline_105K: -32.3%\n210\t    cross_seed_mean_105K: 699\n211\t    cross_seed_nve_mean_105K: 0.63\n212\t  result_rationale: 'Worst-tier 下 C3 在 Walker 内仍 hold，但 variance 更大。Seed 0 (778@105K,\n213\t    85% baseline) 是最优 seed；seed 1-2 预计较低（700/620@105K，76%/68% baseline），因为 subsample\n214\t    OFF + untrained dt_emb 的保护性依赖 RSSM 在 dt=1 数据上的收敛质量——不同 seed 的 RSSM 初始化影响 dt=1\n215\t    prediction 精度，进而影响 value calibration。Normalized v/e 仍一致 低于 1.0x（无 CIVO），但绝对性能比\n216\t    seed 0 差，拉低 cross-seed IQM。 在 worst-tier 下这不影响 C3 的定性结论，但 Agarwal et al. (2021)\n217\t    IQM + CI 会更宽。\n218\t\n219\t    '\n220\t  tables:\n221\t  - title: 008a cross-seed summary\n222\t    headers:\n223\t    - Metric\n224\t    - Seed 0\n225\t    - Seed 1 (pred)\n226\t    - Seed 2 (pred)\n227\t    - Mean\n228\t    rows:\n229\t    - - Eval@105K\n230\t      - '778'\n231\t      - '700'\n232\t      - '620'\n233\t      - '699'\n234\t    - - vs baseline\n235\t      - -15%\n236\t      - -24%\n237\t      - -32%\n238\t      - -24%\n239\t    - - NVE@105K\n240\t      - 0.59x\n241\t      - 0.65x\n242\t      - 0.72x\n243\t      - 0.65x\n244\t    - - Collapse?\n245\t      - 'No'\n246\t      - 'No'\n247\t      - 'No'\n248\t      - 0/3\n249\t  figures_description:\n250\t  - 三 seed 学习曲线叠加，均显示 zigzag 但幅度和收敛点不同\n251\t  analysis: 'C3 在 Walker 内 robust（3/3 seeds NVE<1.0x，无崩溃），但跨 seed 绝对性能变化大 （620-778，22%\n252\t    跨距）。Worst-tier 下，这组数据仅 reinforces Walker-specific 结论。\n253\t\n254\t    '\n255\t- name: Walker Walk 008e_v3 additional seeds (seed 3-4)\n256\t  plan_id: plan_016\n257\t  description: 缩窄 Pathway B collapse probability estimate\n258\t  expected_results:\n259\t    seed3_eval_105K: 830\n260\t    seed3_nve_105K: 0.78\n261\t    seed3_collapse: false\n262\t    seed4_eval_105K: 790\n263\t    seed4_nve_105K: 0.82\n264\t    seed4_collapse: false\n265\t    total_collapse_rate: 1/4 (25%)\n266\t    pathway_b_interpretation: closer to seed variance than systematic pathway\n267\t  result_rationale: 'Worst-tier 核心假设之一：\"Pathway B control experiment reveals 008e_v3_s2\n268\t    collapse was closer to random seed variance than a systematic second pathway\"。Seed\n269\t    3-4 均不崩溃，collapse rate 从 1/2 降至 1/4（25%）。在 4 个 seed 中仅 1 个崩溃， 且该崩溃的机制签名（entropy\n270\t    ↑, eval-driven）与 CIVO 不同，更接近 policy optimization 的随机脆弱性。这削弱 \"multiple vulnerability\n271\t    pathways\" 叙事—— Pathway B 不是 systematic mechanism 而是 seed-specific instability。\n272\t    论文需要 honest reporting：trained dt_emb + dt=1 imag 的 collapse rate ~25%， 无法确定是否显著高于\n273\t    baseline（baseline 0/2 seeds 崩溃，但 n 太小无法做统计检验）。\n274\t\n275\t    '\n276\t  tables:\n277\t  - title: 008e_v3 all seeds\n278\t    headers:\n279\t    - Seed\n280\t    - Eval@105K\n281\t    - NVE@105K\n282\t    - Collapse?\n283\t    - Mechanism\n284\t    rows:\n285\t    - - Seed 1 (s1)\n286\t      - '869.9'\n287\t      - 0.80x\n288\t      - 'No'\n289\t      - '-'\n290\t    - - Seed 2 (s2)\n291\t      - '137.0'\n292\t      - 3.78x\n293\t      - 'Yes'\n294\t      - Eval-driven (Pathway B)\n295\t    - - Seed 3 (pred)\n296\t      - '830'\n297\t      - 0.78x\n298\t      - 'No'\n299\t      - '-'\n300\t    - - Seed 4 (pred)\n301\t      - '790'\n302\t      - 0.82x\n303\t      - 'No'\n304\t      - '-'\n305\t  figures_description:\n306\t  - 4-seed 学习曲线 + NVE 轨迹，标注 seed 2 崩溃点及与其余 3 seeds 的分歧\n307\t  analysis: '1/4 collapse rate 在 worst-tier 下严重削弱 Pathway B 论述。论文可能需要从 \"trained dt_embedding\n308\t    creates vulnerability through multiple pathways\" 退回到 \"trained dt_embedding reliably\n309\t    triggers CIVO (Pathway A, blocked by dt=1 imag); rare policy instability events\n310\t    (1/4 seeds) may or may not be related\"。 这实际上部分 salvages dt=1 mitigation（3/4 seeds\n311\t    成功，接近 baseline）， 但 honest reporting 要求承认 n=4 统计力量不足。\n312\t\n313\t    '\n314\t- name: NVE threshold sensitivity analysis\n315\t  plan_id: plan_034\n316\t  description: 不同 NVE 阈值的分类精度，0 GPU 成本\n317\t  expected_results:\n318\t    walker_only:\n319\t      threshold_1_3x:\n320\t        accuracy: 0.8\n321\t        sensitivity: 1.0\n322\t        specificity: 0.5\n323\t        note: 1 FP (009c@25K NVE=1.26 borderline, 但 35K+ 限定后为 TN)\n324\t      threshold_1_5x:\n325\t        accuracy: 1.0\n326\t        sensitivity: 1.0\n327\t        specificity: 1.0\n328\t        note: 4/4 perfect at 35K+\n329\t      threshold_1_7x:\n330\t        accuracy: 0.8\n331\t        sensitivity: 0.67\n332\t        specificity: 1.0\n333\t        note: 009b peak NVE=1.62x barely above 1.7x? Actually no, 1.62<1.7 → FN\n334\t      threshold_2_0x:\n335\t        accuracy: 0.8\n336\t        sensitivity: 0.67\n337\t        specificity: 1.0\n338\t        note: 009b peak 2.05x@25K excluded by 35K+ rule; 1.62x@45K<2.0 → FN\n339\t      auroc: 0.98\n340\t    cross_env_walker_cheetah:\n341\t      threshold_1_5x:\n342\t        accuracy: 0.64\n343\t        sensitivity: 0.4\n344\t        specificity: 1.0\n345\t        note: Walker 2/2 trained→TP; Cheetah 0/3 trained→FN; all untrained→TN\n346\t      auroc: 0.72\n347\t    cross_env_all_three:\n348\t      threshold_1_5x:\n349\t        accuracy: 0.58\n350\t        sensitivity: 0.29\n351\t        specificity: 1.0\n352\t        note: 仅 Walker 2/7 trained seeds 被检出\n353\t      auroc: 0.65\n354\t  result_rationale: 'Walker 内 1.5x threshold 完美分离（AUROC~0.98），这是 existing data 的强结论。\n355\t    但在 worst-tier 下，Cheetah 的 trained dt_emb seeds NVE 全部 <1.5x（范围 0.8-1.4x）， 因为 Cheetah\n356\t    的 RSSM fidelity characteristics 不同——reward density 更高、state dynamics 更 smooth，dt_emb\n357\t    的 observation decoder 梯度不产生同样的 systematic bias。 这导致 threshold 在 Cheetah 上产生大量\n358\t    false negatives（degradation 发生但 NVE 不超标）。Cross-env AUROC 从 0.98 降至 ~0.72，远低于 diagnostic\n359\t    tool 的实用标准。 论文必须 honest report：\"NVE>1.5x is a reliable Walker Walk diagnostic\n360\t    but does NOT generalize to Cheetah Run, where degradation manifests through different\n361\t    dynamics.\"\n362\t\n363\t    '\n364\t  tables:\n365\t  - title: NVE 1.5x threshold cross-environment performance\n366\t    headers:\n367\t    - Environment\n368\t    - Trained Seeds\n369\t    - TP\n370\t    - FN\n371\t    - Untrained Seeds\n372\t    - TN\n373\t    - FP\n374\t    - Accuracy\n375\t    rows:\n376\t    - - Walker Walk\n377\t      - '3'\n378\t      - '3'\n379\t      - '0'\n380\t      - '2'\n381\t      - '2'\n382\t      - '0'\n383\t      - 5/5=1.00\n384\t    - - Cheetah Run\n385\t      - '3'\n386\t      - '0'\n387\t      - '3'\n388\t      - '3'\n389\t      - '3'\n390\t      - '0'\n391\t      - 3/6=0.50\n392\t    - - Cartpole Swingup\n393\t      - '3'\n394\t      - '0'\n395\t      - '3'\n396\t      - '3'\n397\t      - '3'\n398\t      - '0'\n399\t      - 3/6=0.50\n400\t    - - Cross-env total\n401\t      - '9'\n402\t      - '3'\n403\t      - '6'\n404\t      - '8'\n405\t      - '8'\n406\t      - '0'\n407\t      - 11/17=0.65\n408\t  figures_description:\n409\t  - ROC 曲线：Walker-only (AUROC=0.98) vs cross-env (AUROC=0.72)\n410\t  analysis: 'NVE 方法论是 worst-tier 下论文的 second contribution pillar，但必须诚实定位为 \"validated\n411\t    in Walker Walk, proposed for broader adoption with caveats\"。跨环境失败 不否定方法论本身——而是揭示\n412\t    CIVO 机制的 environment-specificity。论文应讨论 为何 Cheetah 的 NVE pattern 不同（reward density、RSSM\n413\t    fidelity characteristics）， 将 negative result 转化为 diagnostic insight。\n414\t\n415\t    '\n416\t- name: Cheetah Run baseline (3 seeds)\n417\t  plan_id: plan_020\n418\t  description: 第二 DMC 环境的 dt=1 baseline\n419\t  expected_results:\n420\t    seed1_final_eval: 849.8\n421\t    seed1_status: DONE (exp_010a)\n422\t    seed2_final_eval: 825\n423\t    seed3_final_eval: 862\n424\t    cross_seed_mean: 846\n425\t    cross_seed_std: 19\n426\t    ve_ratio_stable: 0.65-0.72 from 135K+\n427\t    ve_ratio_trajectory:\n428\t      25K: 0.09\n429\t      35K: 0.19\n430\t      45K: 0.28\n431\t      55K: 0.36\n432\t      65K: 0.47\n433\t      75K: 0.57\n434\t      85K: 0.63\n435\t      95K: 0.66\n436\t      105K: 0.68\n437\t  result_rationale: 'Cheetah Run baseline 在 DreamerV3 上训练正常，peak ~850。Seed 1 已完成（849.8）。\n438\t    Cheetah 的 reward 是 forward velocity（dense, smooth），收敛特性与 Walker Walk 类似 但 v/e\n439\t    trajectory 略低（Cheetah 的 discount structure 和 reward scale 不同）。 Baseline 本身不受 worst-tier\n440\t    影响——环境正常运行是所有后续实验的前提。\n441\t\n442\t    '\n443\t  tables: []\n444\t  figures_description: []\n445\t  analysis: 'Baseline 确立 Cheetah Run 的参考线。v/e calibration（~0.68@105K）与 Walker（~0.656@105K）\n446\t    高度一致，为 NVE 比较提供合理基础。\n447\t\n448\t    '\n449\t- name: Cheetah Run trained dt_emb + subsample ON (3 seeds)\n450\t  plan_id: plan_021\n451\t  description: 复现 CIVO collapse in Cheetah — worst-tier 预测失败\n452\t  expected_results:\n453\t    seed0:\n454\t      eval_trajectory:\n455\t        5K: 31\n456\t        15K: 190\n457\t        25K: 370\n458\t        35K: 520\n459\t        45K: 490\n460\t        55K: 440\n461\t        65K: 400\n462\t        75K: 380\n463\t        85K: 360\n464\t        95K: 370\n465\t        105K: 385\n466\t      value_trajectory:\n467\t        25K: 28\n468\t        35K: 85\n469\t        45K: 120\n470\t        55K: 140\n471\t        65K: 145\n472\t        75K: 140\n473\t        85K: 130\n474\t        95K: 125\n475\t        105K: 128\n476\t      nve_trajectory:\n477\t        35K: 0.94\n478\t        45K: 0.92\n479\t        55K: 0.95\n480\t        65K: 0.83\n481\t        75K: 0.72\n482\t        85K: 0.68\n483\t        95K: 0.65\n484\t        105K: 0.63\n485\t      collapse: false\n486\t      peak_nve: 0.95\n487\t      pattern: gradual decline without value acceleration\n488\t    seed1:\n489\t      eval_trajectory:\n490\t        35K: 480\n491\t        45K: 430\n492\t        55K: 380\n493\t        65K: 350\n494\t        75K: 340\n495\t        85K: 360\n496\t        95K: 375\n497\t        105K: 390\n498\t      nve_trajectory:\n499\t        35K: 1.25\n500\t        45K: 1.3\n501\t        55K: 1.28\n502\t        65K: 1.15\n503\t        75K: 0.98\n504\t        85K: 0.92\n505\t        95K: 0.88\n506\t        105K: 0.85\n507\t      collapse: false\n508\t      peak_nve: 1.3\n509\t      pattern: mild overestimation plateau then decline — not accelerating\n510\t    seed2:\n511\t      eval_trajectory:\n512\t        35K: 550\n513\t        45K: 520\n514\t        55K: 470\n515\t        65K: 430\n516\t        75K: 410\n517\t        85K: 420\n518\t        95K: 430\n519\t        105K: 445\n520\t      nve_trajectory:\n521\t        35K: 0.82\n522\t        45K: 0.85\n523\t        55K: 0.9\n524\t        65K: 0.87\n525\t        75K: 0.8\n526\t        85K: 0.78\n527\t        95K: 0.75\n528\t        105K: 0.74\n529\t      collapse: false\n530\t      peak_nve: 0.9\n531\t      pattern: value suppression — similar to Walker dt=4\n532\t    cross_seed_collapse_rate: 0/3\n533\t    cross_seed_nve_max: 1.3\n534\t    cross_seed_nve_mean_at_55K: 1.04\n535\t    cross_seed_eval_mean_105K: 407\n536\t    vs_baseline_105K: -52%\n537\t  result_rationale: \"Worst-tier 核心假设：\\\"Cheetah Run shows performance degradation with\\\n538\t    \\ dt>1 but NVE pattern differs\\\"。三个 seed 均显示 degradation（eval 407 平均 vs baseline\\\n539\t    \\ 846，-52%），但 NVE 模式与 Walker 定性不同： (1) Seed 0 (NVE 0.63-0.95x)：value suppression\\\n540\t    \\ 模式，类似 Walker dt=4——RSSM 在\\n    Cheetah 的 dt>1 prediction 质量差导致 critic underestimate\\\n541\t    \\ 而非 overestimate。\\n    Cheetah 的 velocity-based reward 结构使 dt>1 reward prediction\\\n542\t    \\ 偏差方向不同。\\n(2) Seed 1 (NVE peak 1.30x)：温和过估计但不加速。NVE 在 35-55K 达到 1.25-1.30x\\n\\\n543\t    \\    后自行下降至 0.85x。与 Walker 008d 的加速发散（1.71x→2.09x→4.12x）形成鲜明对比。\\n    Cheetah 的\\\n544\t    \\ RSSM 可能在 dt>1 有更好的 self-correction 能力（state space 更规则）。\\n(3) Seed 2 (NVE 0.74-0.90x)：纯\\\n545\t    \\ value suppression。 没有任何 seed 的 NVE 超过 1.5x → 1.5x threshold 在 Cheetah 上完全失效（0/3\\\n546\t    \\ detected）。 Degradation 确实存在但不是 CIVO——更可能是 learning signal reduction (C5) + RSSM\\\n547\t    \\ fidelity gap 的混合效应，不伴随 positive feedback loop。\\n\"\n548\t  tables:\n549\t  - title: Cheetah CIVO trigger cross-seed NVE\n550\t    headers:\n551\t    - Step\n552\t    - Seed 0 NVE\n553\t    - Seed 1 NVE\n554\t    - Seed 2 NVE\n555\t    - Walker 008d NVE (ref)\n556\t    rows:\n557\t    - - 35K\n558\t      - '0.94'\n559\t      - '1.25'\n560\t      - '0.82'\n561\t      - '1.71'\n562\t    - - 45K\n563\t      - '0.92'\n564\t      - '1.30'\n565\t      - '0.85'\n566\t      - '2.09'\n567\t    - - 55K\n568\t      - '0.95'\n569\t      - '1.28'\n570\t      - '0.90'\n571\t      - '4.12'\n572\t    - - 65K\n573\t      - '0.83'\n574\t      - '1.15'\n575\t      - '0.87'\n576\t      - (collapsed)\n577\t    - - 105K\n578\t      - '0.63'\n579\t      - '0.85'\n580\t      - '0.74'\n581\t      - '-'\n582\t  figures_description:\n583\t  - Cheetah vs Walker NVE 轨迹对比：Walker 加速发散 vs Cheetah 平稳/下降\n584\t  - Cheetah 3-seed eval 曲线 + baseline reference\n585\t  analysis: '这是 worst-tier 的 defining result。Degradation 存在但 CIVO 缺失。论文必须承认： \"The\n586\t    CIVO mechanism (accelerating NVE feedback loop) is environment-specific. In Cheetah\n587\t    Run, trained dt_embedding degrades performance through a different mechanism —\n588\t    likely learning signal quality degradation without the positive feedback loop\n589\t    observed in Walker.\" Limitations section 需讨论 Cheetah 为何不同：(a) reward 结构（pure velocity\n590\t    vs complex locomotion reward），(b) state space dimensionality 和 smoothness， (c)\n591\t    RSSM 对不同 dynamics 的 fidelity characteristics。\n592\t\n593\t    '\n594\t- name: Cheetah Run dt_embed_dim=0 + subsample ON (3 seeds)\n595\t  plan_id: plan_022\n596\t  description: Cheetah 因果控制——worst-tier 预测无 clean separation\n597\t  expected_results:\n598\t    seed0:\n599\t      eval_trajectory:\n600\t        35K: 470\n601\t        55K: 400\n602\t        75K: 370\n603\t        105K: 410\n604\t      nve_trajectory:\n605\t        35K: 0.75\n606\t        55K: 0.9\n607\t        75K: 0.85\n608\t        105K: 0.7\n609\t      pattern: similar degradation to trained dt_emb\n610\t    seed1:\n611\t      eval_trajectory:\n612\t        35K: 510\n613\t        55K: 430\n614\t        75K: 400\n615\t        105K: 440\n616\t      nve_trajectory:\n617\t        35K: 0.68\n618\t        55K: 0.8\n619\t        75K: 0.75\n620\t        105K: 0.65\n621\t    seed2:\n622\t      eval_trajectory:\n623\t        35K: 490\n624\t        55K: 420\n625\t        75K: 380\n626\t        105K: 380\n627\t      nve_trajectory:\n628\t        35K: 1.1\n629\t        55K: 1.05\n630\t        75K: 0.9\n631\t        105K: 0.82\n632\t    cross_seed_eval_mean_105K: 410\n633\t    cross_seed_nve_range:\n634\t    - 0.65\n635\t    - 1.1\n636\t    nve_overlap_with_trained: substantial (trained range [0.63, 1.30] vs untrained\n637\t      [0.65, 1.10])\n638\t    vs_trained_dt_emb_eval_diff: +0.7% (not significant)\n639\t  result_rationale: 'Worst-tier 假设：\"NVE 1.5x threshold doesn''t separate trained/untrained\n640\t    in Cheetah\"。 去掉 dt_embedding 后 Cheetah 的 eval 和 NVE 与 trained dt_emb 配置几乎无差异 （eval\n641\t    410 vs 407, NVE 0.65-1.10 vs 0.63-1.30）。原因：Cheetah 的 degradation 根源是 learning\n642\t    signal reduction（subsample ON 导致有效 transition 数减半）而非 dt_embedding-driven CIVO。在\n643\t    Walker 中，去掉 dt_emb 阻止了 CIVO feedback loop， 产生 dramatic 差异（008f NVE<1.0 vs 008d\n644\t    NVE>2.0）；在 Cheetah 中，没有 CIVO feedback loop 需要阻止，所以去掉 dt_emb 不产生 significant effect。\n645\t    这是 worst-tier 下最难处理的结果——直接否定 C2 因果链在 Cheetah 上的适用性。\n646\t\n647\t    '\n648\t  tables:\n649\t  - title: 'Cheetah: trained vs no dt_emb'\n650\t    headers:\n651\t    - Metric\n652\t    - Trained dt_emb (plan_021)\n653\t    - No dt_emb (plan_022)\n654\t    - Δ\n655\t    rows:\n656\t    - - Eval mean@105K\n657\t      - '407'\n658\t      - '410'\n659\t      - +0.7% (ns)\n660\t    - - NVE range (35K+)\n661\t      - '[0.63, 1.30]'\n662\t      - '[0.65, 1.10]'\n663\t      - overlapping\n664\t    - - Collapse rate\n665\t      - 0/3\n666\t      - 0/3\n667\t      - identical\n668\t    - - NVE>1.5x rate\n669\t      - 0/3\n670\t      - 0/3\n671\t      - identical\n672\t  figures_description:\n673\t  - 'Cheetah trained vs untrained dt_emb: eval + NVE 并排对比，标注 overlap region'\n674\t  analysis: 'Cheetah 的 \"no separation\" 是 worst-tier 最 damaging 的 cross-env negative\n675\t    result。 论文需要解释为什么 Walker 的因果机制不 transfer：dt_embedding 在 Cheetah 的 observation\n676\t    decoder 梯度路径可能不产生同向 systematic bias，因为 Cheetah 的 state space structure（关节速度为主导\n677\t    observable）让 RSSM 对 dt>1 的 prediction error 分布更 uniform（不集中在特定 decoder head），无法形成\n678\t    amplification loop。\n679\t\n680\t    '\n681\t- name: Cheetah Run untrained dt_emb + no subsample (3 seeds)\n682\t  plan_id: plan_023\n683\t  description: Cheetah value growth suppression — worst-tier 预测无 clear advantage\n684\t  expected_results:\n685\t    seed0:\n686\t      eval_trajectory:\n687\t        35K: 490\n688\t        55K: 430\n689\t        75K: 450\n690\t        105K: 520\n691\t      nve_trajectory:\n692\t        35K: 0.8\n693\t        55K: 0.75\n694\t        75K: 0.7\n695\t        105K: 0.65\n696\t    seed1:\n697\t      eval_trajectory:\n698\t        35K: 520\n699\t        55K: 460\n700\t        75K: 480\n701\t        105K: 550\n702\t      nve_trajectory:\n703\t        35K: 0.72\n704\t        55K: 0.78\n705\t        75K: 0.68\n706\t        105K: 0.6\n707\t    seed2:\n708\t      eval_trajectory:\n709\t        35K: 480\n710\t        55K: 440\n711\t        75K: 430\n712\t        105K: 490\n713\t      nve_trajectory:\n714\t        35K: 0.85\n715\t        55K: 0.82\n716\t        75K: 0.75\n717\t        105K: 0.7\n718\t    cross_seed_eval_mean_105K: 520\n719\t    vs_baseline: -39%\n720\t    vs_trained_dt_emb: +28% (520 vs 407)\n721\t    vs_no_dt_emb: +27% (520 vs 410)\n722\t  result_rationale: 'Subsample OFF 保留完整 learning signal，所以 eval 高于 plan_021/022（520\n723\t    vs 407/410）。 但这个提升来自 learning signal preservation（C5），不是 value suppression（C3）。\n724\t    NVE 在 0.60-0.85x 范围，与 plan_022 (0.65-1.10) 有 overlap。Worst-tier 解读： C3 在 Cheetah\n725\t    上不能 cleanly 验证，因为 baseline comparison 被 subsample 差异混淆。 To isolate C3 需要 subsample\n726\t    ON + untrained dt_emb（但 Walker 已有 008c/008e_v3 数据做此对比）。在 Cheetah 上，所有 dt>1 配置都\n727\t    degrades，无论 dt_emb 状态如何。\n728\t\n729\t    '\n730\t  tables: []\n731\t  figures_description: []\n732\t  analysis: 'Cheetah untrained dt_emb 的 eval 提升主要归因于 subsample OFF（保留学习信号）， 非 value\n733\t    suppression 机制。C3 声明在 Cheetah 上 confounded。\n734\t\n735\t    '\n736\t- name: Cartpole Swingup baseline (3 seeds)\n737\t  plan_id: plan_050\n738\t  description: 非 locomotion 环境 baseline\n739\t  expected_results:\n740\t    seed0_final_eval: 840\n741\t    seed1_final_eval: 820\n742\t    seed2_final_eval: 855\n743\t    cross_seed_mean: 838\n744\t    ve_ratio_stable: 0.60-0.68 from 135K+\n745\t  result_rationale: 'Cartpole Swingup 是 DreamerV3 上的 well-solved benchmark，baseline\n746\t    ~840。 V/e ratio 收敛到 ~0.64，略低于 Walker/Cheetah，因为 Cartpole 的 sparse initial reward（swingup\n747\t    前 reward 极低）使 value function 在 early training 更保守。\n748\t\n749\t    '\n750\t  tables: []\n751\t  figures_description: []\n752\t  analysis: 'Baseline 正常。Cartpole 的 non-locomotion dynamics（pendulum + cart） 为跨环境泛化测试提供了不同\n753\t    task family。\n754\t\n755\t    '\n756\t- name: Cartpole Swingup trained dt_emb + subsample ON (3 seeds)\n757\t  plan_id: plan_051\n758\t  description: 复现 CIVO collapse in Cartpole — worst-tier 预测 no CIVO\n759\t  expected_results:\n760\t    seed0:\n761\t      eval_105K: 320\n762\t      peak_nve: 0.75\n763\t      pattern: value suppression — critic under-estimates\n764\t    seed1:\n765\t      eval_105K: 280\n766\t      peak_nve: 0.9\n767\t      pattern: learning failure — low asymptote\n768\t    seed2:\n769\t      eval_105K: 350\n770\t      peak_nve: 0.65\n771\t      pattern: value suppression\n772\t    cross_seed_eval_mean: 317\n773\t    vs_baseline: -62%\n774\t    collapse_rate: 0/3\n775\t    nve_max: 0.9\n776\t    nve_gt_1_5x: 0/3\n777\t  result_rationale: \"Cartpole Swingup 的 sparse reward structure 使 dt>1 transitions\\\n778\t    \\ 的 reward prediction 几乎无信息（swingup 前大量 near-zero reward）。Trained dt_emb 不会产生\\\n779\t    \\ CIVO 因为： (1) RSSM 对 dt>1 的 reward prediction 偏差方向是 under-estimation（sparse reward\\n\\\n780\t    \\    的高 reward events 在 dt>1 步后更难预测，导致 systematic negative bias）；\\n(2) Observation\\\n781\t    \\ decoder 梯度集中在 pendulum angle 上（单一关键 observable），\\n    不像 Walker 的 multi-head\\\n782\t    \\ gradient（orientations/velocity/height）能形成\\n    amplification；\\n(3) Cartpole\\\n783\t    \\ 的 state space（4D: cart pos/vel + pole angle/vel）远小于\\n    Walker（24D+），RSSM 的\\\n784\t    \\ dt>1 fidelity gap 更小。\\n结果是 degradation 但以 value suppression/learning failure\\\n785\t    \\ 形式出现，无 CIVO signature。\\n\"\n786\t  tables:\n787\t  - title: Cartpole trained dt_emb NVE\n788\t    headers:\n789\t    - Seed\n790\t    - Peak NVE\n791\t    - NVE@105K\n792\t    - Collapse?\n793\t    - Pattern\n794\t    rows:\n795\t    - - '0'\n796\t      - '0.75'\n797\t      - '0.60'\n798\t      - 'No'\n799\t      - Value suppression\n800\t    - - '1'\n801\t      - '0.90'\n802\t      - '0.70'\n803\t      - 'No'\n804\t      - Learning failure\n805\t    - - '2'\n806\t      - '0.65'\n807\t      - '0.55'\n808\t      - 'No'\n809\t      - Value suppression\n810\t  figures_description: []\n811\t  analysis: 'Cartpole 的 NVE pattern（全部 <1.0x）与 Walker 的 CIVO（>1.5x accelerating）和\n812\t    Cheetah 的 mixed pattern（0.6-1.3x stable）都不同。三个环境三种 failure mode： Walker=CIVO,\n813\t    Cheetah=mild overestimation/plateau, Cartpole=value suppression。 这证明 dt>1 degradation\n814\t    是 universal 但 mechanism 是 environment-specific。\n815\t\n816\t    '\n817\t- name: Cartpole Swingup dt_embed_dim=0 + subsample ON (3 seeds)\n818\t  plan_id: plan_052\n819\t  description: Cartpole 因果控制\n820\t  expected_results:\n821\t    seed0_eval_105K: 310\n822\t    seed1_eval_105K: 290\n823\t    seed2_eval_105K: 340\n824\t    cross_seed_eval_mean: 313\n825\t    vs_trained_dt_emb: -1.3% (not significant)\n826\t    nve_range:\n827\t    - 0.55\n828\t    - 0.85\n829\t    nve_overlap_with_trained: complete overlap\n830\t  result_rationale: '与 Cheetah 类似，去掉 dt_embedding 在 Cartpole 上不产生 significant 差异。\n831\t    Degradation 根源是 learning signal reduction（C5），dt_emb 不是 primary factor。 Eval 313\n832\t    vs trained 317，差异在噪声范围内。NVE 完全 overlap。 Walker 中 008f vs 008d 的 dramatic 差异（NVE\n833\t    0.97x vs 2.09x）在 Cartpole 不可复现——因为 Cartpole 没有 CIVO feedback loop 需要 dt_emb 来\n834\t    trigger。\n835\t\n836\t    '\n837\t  tables: []\n838\t  figures_description: []\n839\t  analysis: 'Cartpole 的 \"no separation\" 进一步确认：CIVO 是 Walker-specific phenomenon。 Cross-env\n840\t    data 现在显示 3 environments 中仅 1 个有 CIVO。\n841\t\n842\t    '\n843\t- name: 'RSSM prediction quality: dt=1 vs dt=2 transitions'\n844\t  plan_id: plan_030\n845\t  description: 量化 RSSM fidelity gap 的 environment-specific characteristics\n846\t  expected_results:\n847\t    cheetah_baseline:\n848\t      dt1_obs_mse: 10.2\n849\t      dt2_obs_mse: 18.5\n850\t      obs_gap: 1.81\n851\t      dt1_reward_mae: 0.008\n852\t      dt2_reward_mae: 0.012\n853\t      reward_gap: 1.5\n854\t    cheetah_trained_dt_emb:\n855\t      dt1_obs_mse: 15.8\n856\t      dt2_obs_mse: 22.3\n857\t      obs_gap: 1.41\n858\t      dt1_reward_mae: 0.035\n859\t      dt2_reward_mae: 0.065\n860\t      reward_gap: 1.86\n861\t    cheetah_no_dt_emb:\n862\t      dt1_obs_mse: 9.5\n863\t      dt2_obs_mse: 19.8\n864\t      obs_gap: 2.08\n865\t      dt1_reward_mae: 0.52\n866\t      dt2_reward_mae: 0.54\n867\t      reward_gap: 1.04\n868\t    walker_vs_cheetah_obs_gap_comparison:\n869\t      walker_baseline: 2.04\n870\t      cheetah_baseline: 1.81\n871\t      walker_trained: 1.3\n872\t      cheetah_trained: 1.41\n873\t  result_rationale: \"Cheetah 的 RSSM fidelity gap 与 Walker 数值接近但分布不同。关键差异： (1) Cheetah\\\n874\t    \\ 的 trained dt_emb reward gap (1.86x) 低于 Walker (2.78x)——\\n    Cheetah 的 velocity\\\n875\t    \\ reward 更 smooth，dt_emb 不会像 Walker 那样在 reward head\\n    产生 large systematic bias。但注意\\\n876\t    \\ Walker 的 reward gradient = 0（by architecture），\\n    所以 reward gap 不是 CIVO 的直接驱动因素。\\n\\\n877\t    (2) Cheetah 的 obs_gap (1.81x baseline, 1.41x trained) 与 Walker (2.04x, 1.30x)\\\n878\t    \\ \\n    类似，但 obs MSE 的绝对值更低——Cheetah 的 state space 更规则，RSSM 建模质量更好。\\n(3) Cheetah\\\n879\t    \\ trained dt_emb 的 dt1 abs obs_MSE (15.8) 显著低于 Walker (41.31)——\\n    模型没有像 Walker\\\n880\t    \\ 那样因为 CIVO 而全面崩塌。\\nWorst-tier 解读：fidelity gap 存在但不 sufficient to trigger CIVO\\\n881\t    \\ in Cheetah。 机制的 environment-specificity 体现在 fidelity gap 如何通过 gradient pathways\\\n882\t    \\ 传播到 value function——Walker 的 multi-head gradient structure 放大 bias， Cheetah\\\n883\t    \\ 的更 uniform gradient 不放大。\\n\"\n884\t  tables:\n885\t  - title: Cross-environment RSSM fidelity comparison\n886\t    headers:\n887\t    - Model\n888\t    - Env\n889\t    - dt1 obs_MSE\n890\t    - dt2 obs_MSE\n891\t    - obs gap\n892\t    - reward gap\n893\t    rows:\n894\t    - - Baseline\n895\t      - Walker\n896\t      - '13.49'\n897\t      - '27.50'\n898\t      - 2.04x\n899\t      - 1.56x\n900\t    - - Baseline\n901\t      - Cheetah\n902\t      - '10.2'\n903\t      - '18.5'\n904\t      - 1.81x\n905\t      - 1.50x\n906\t    - - Trained dt_emb\n907\t      - Walker\n908\t      - '41.31'\n909\t      - '53.67'\n910\t      - 1.30x\n911\t      - 2.78x\n912\t    - - Trained dt_emb\n913\t      - Cheetah\n914\t      - '15.8'\n915\t      - '22.3'\n916\t      - 1.41x\n917\t      - 1.86x\n918\t    - - No dt_emb\n919\t      - Walker\n920\t      - '8.01'\n921\t      - '22.04'\n922\t      - 2.75x\n923\t      - 1.01x\n924\t    - - No dt_emb\n925\t      - Cheetah\n926\t      - '9.5'\n927\t      - '19.8'\n928\t      - 2.08x\n929\t      - 1.04x\n930\t  figures_description:\n931\t  - 'Cross-env RSSM fidelity heatmap: obs_MSE × reward_MAE 四象限，标注 CIVO/non-CIVO regions'\n932\t  analysis: 'RSSM fidelity gap 是 necessary but not sufficient for CIVO。Cheetah 有 gap\n933\t    但 无 CIVO 放大。论文需讨论 gradient pathway structure 作为 missing mediator。\n934\t\n935\t    '\n936\t- name: Actor entropy analysis\n937\t  plan_id: plan_031\n938\t  description: Walker + Cheetah actor entropy trajectory 对比\n939\t  expected_results:\n940\t    walker_civo_collapsed_008d:\n941\t      entropy_trajectory: 8.2→-1.9→-3.5→-4.6→-4.9\n942\t      pattern: 'entropy ↓: policy becomes deterministic during CIVO'\n943\t    walker_pathway_b_008e_v3_s2:\n944\t      entropy_trajectory: -5.1→-5.2→-5.2→-4.5→-3.8\n945\t      pattern: 'entropy ↑: policy destabilizes (opposite of CIVO)'\n946\t    walker_healthy_008a:\n947\t      entropy_trajectory: -4.2→-4.5→-4.6→-4.7→-4.8\n948\t      pattern: 'entropy stable: normal policy convergence'\n949\t    cheetah_trained_dt_emb:\n950\t      entropy_trajectory: -3.8→-4.0→-4.1→-4.2→-4.3\n951\t      pattern: 'entropy stable: no CIVO or Pathway B signature'\n952\t    cheetah_no_dt_emb:\n953\t      entropy_trajectory: -3.7→-3.9→-4.0→-4.1→-4.2\n954\t      pattern: 'entropy stable: indistinguishable from trained'\n955\t  result_rationale: 'Actor entropy 在 Walker 中是 CIVO 和 Pathway B 的 discriminating signature：\n956\t    CIVO → entropy ↓（critic overestimate 让 actor converge to exploitative policy），\n957\t    Pathway B → entropy ↑（policy destabilization，actor 失去 coherent strategy）。 在 Cheetah\n958\t    中，因为没有 CIVO 或 Pathway B，所有配置的 entropy trajectory  几乎一致（stable decline），无法作为 diagnostic\n959\t    tool。这进一步确认 Cheetah 的 degradation 机制不同——没有 actor 层面的 pathological dynamics。\n960\t\n961\t    '\n962\t  tables: []\n963\t  figures_description:\n964\t  - Walker entropy 三轨对比（CIVO↓ / Pathway B↑ / healthy→）vs Cheetah 无差异\n965\t  analysis: 'Entropy analysis 在 Walker 内是有力 diagnostic，但在 Cheetah 上无差异性。 论文可呈现为 Walker-specific\n966\t    finding。\n967\t\n968\t    '\n969\t- name: Value prediction distribution vs realized returns\n970\t  plan_id: plan_032\n971\t  description: V(s) vs MC return 分布分析\n972\t  expected_results:\n973\t    walker_008d_divergence:\n974\t      value_mean: 97.5\n975\t      mc_return_mean: 35\n976\t      ks_statistic: 0.72\n977\t      pattern: right-shifted value distribution — systematic overestimation\n978\t    walker_008a_calibration:\n979\t      value_mean: 280\n980\t      mc_return_mean: 550\n981\t      ks_statistic: 0.35\n982\t      pattern: left-shifted but not pathological — conservative value\n983\t    cheetah_trained_divergence:\n984\t      value_mean: 140\n985\t      mc_return_mean: 180\n986\t      ks_statistic: 0.28\n987\t      pattern: mild underestimation — no systematic overestimation\n988\t  result_rationale: 'Walker 008d 的 V(s) 分布系统性右偏（overestimate），与 MC return 严重脱节 （KS=0.72）。这是\n989\t    CIVO 的 direct evidence。Cheetah trained dt_emb 的 V(s) 分布仅轻微左偏（underestimate, KS=0.28），不存在\n990\t    systematic overestimation。 Worst-tier 下，分布分析强化了 \"CIVO is Walker-specific\" 的结论。\n991\t\n992\t    '\n993\t  tables: []\n994\t  figures_description:\n995\t  - 'V(s) vs MC return 散点图 + violin plot: Walker 008d (divergent) vs Cheetah (aligned)'\n996\t  analysis: '分布分析是比 v/e ratio 更 informative 的 proxy，但在 worst-tier 下仅确认 已知结论。投入 1 GPU-hour\n997\t    的 ROI 有限。\n998\t\n999\t    '\n1000\t- name: dt_embedding cosine similarity analysis\n1001\t  plan_id: plan_033\n1002\t  description: learned dt_emb vectors 的 dt=1 vs dt=2 similarity evolution\n1003\t  expected_results:\n1004\t    walker_initial_cosine: 0.85\n1005\t    walker_trained_30K_cosine: 0.42\n1006\t    walker_trained_60K_cosine: 0.28\n1007\t    walker_trend: diverging — dt=1 and dt=2 embeddings become increasingly dissimilar\n1008\t    cheetah_initial_cosine: 0.85\n1009\t    cheetah_trained_30K_cosine: 0.55\n1010\t    cheetah_trained_60K_cosine: 0.48\n1011\t    cheetah_trend: partial divergence — less separation than Walker\n1012\t  result_rationale: 'Walker 中 dt_emb 的 dt=1 和 dt=2 vectors 快速分化（cosine 0.85→0.28），\n1013\t    说明 network 积极利用 dt conditioning 来做 specialized predictions——这是 CIVO 的前提条件。Cheetah\n1014\t    中分化较缓（0.85→0.48），说明 dt_emb 被利用程度 较低——network 未充分 specialize on dt information，因此不会形成\n1015\t    strong dt-dependent value bias。这与 Cheetah 的 observation decoder 梯度更 uniform 的假设一致——没有足够的\n1016\t    gradient signal 来 push dt_emb 向 high-separation direction。\n1017\t\n1018\t    '\n1019\t  tables: []\n1020\t  figures_description:\n1021\t  - 'dt_emb cosine similarity vs training step: Walker (fast divergence) vs Cheetah\n1022\t    (slow)'\n1023\t  analysis: 'Cosine analysis 提供了为什么 CIVO 在 Cheetah 不发生的 additional mechanistic insight：\n1024\t    dt_embedding 在 Cheetah 中学到的 dt 区分度更低，减少了 condition-dependent bias 的 severity。可作为\n1025\t    Discussion section 的 supporting analysis。0 GPU cost，值得做。\n1026\t\n1027\t    '\n1028\t- name: Uncertainty-gated imagination truncation pilot\n1029\t  plan_id: plan_060\n1030\t  description: RSSM 不确定性门控 imagination 截断——Walker Walk pilot\n1031\t  expected_results:\n1032\t    eval_105K: 540\n1033\t    vs_baseline: -41%\n1034\t    nve_peak: 1.15\n1035\t    collapse: false\n1036\t    truncation_rate_at_dt2: 0.35\n1037\t    effective_horizon_mean: 11.2\n1038\t    issues:\n1039\t    - RSSM ensemble disagreement 校准不准——在 dt=1 transitions 上也频繁触发截断\n1040\t    - 有效 horizon 从 15 降至 ~11，减少了 long-range credit assignment\n1041\t    - 稳定但性能远低于 008e_v3 seed 1 (870) 和 baseline (916)\n1042\t  result_rationale: 'RSSM 本身不提供 well-calibrated uncertainty estimates（DreamerV3 使用\n1043\t    single RSSM， 不是 ensemble）。Pilot 需要额外实现 RSSM ensemble 或使用 KL divergence as proxy。\n1044\t    在 worst-tier 下，uncertainty estimate 噪声大：dt=1 transitions 的不确定性 也偶尔偏高（false truncation），而\n1045\t    dt>1 transitions 的不确定性不总是偏高 （missed truncation）。Net effect: truncation 防止了最严重的\n1046\t    collapse（NVE 不超 1.5x）， 但 over-truncation 缩短有效 horizon，损失 long-range learning signal。\n1047\t    Eval 540 好于 008d collapse (83) 但远低于 008e_v3 success (870)。 不适合作为 paper contribution——implementation\n1048\t    complexity 高但 benefit 有限。\n1049\t\n1050\t    '\n1051\t  tables: []\n1052\t  figures_description: []\n1053\t  analysis: 'Uncertainty truncation 是 \"reasonable but noisy\" 的 mitigation。在 worst-tier\n1054\t    下 不足以写入论文——更适合 future work section 的 one-sentence mention。 CoRL deadline 前不值得投入更多\n1055\t    GPU。\n1056\t\n1057\t    '\n1058\t- name: Hopper Hop validation (3 seeds × 3 configs)\n1059\t  plan_id: plan_040\n1060\t  description: 第三 DMC locomotion 环境——worst-tier 预测：P2 优先级，可能不跑\n1061\t  expected_results:\n1062\t    likely_status: NOT RUN before CoRL deadline (P2 priority)\n1063\t    if_run:\n1064\t      baseline_mean: 250\n1065\t      trained_dt_emb_mean: 120\n1066\t      trained_dt_emb_nve_pattern: mixed — some seeds >1.0x, none >1.5x\n1067\t      no_dt_emb_mean: 130\n1068\t      separation: minimal\n1069\t  result_rationale: 'Hopper Hop 是 sparse reward + contact-rich dynamics，DreamerV3\n1070\t    baseline 仅 ~250 （远低于 Walker/Cheetah）。在 worst-tier 下，即使跑了，低 baseline 性能使得 v/e ratio\n1071\t    极不稳定（分母小），NVE 信噪比差，无法得出 clean 结论。 此外，45 GPU-hours 的预算在 13 天 deadline 前不值得投入——这些资源应用于\n1072\t    确保 Walker 数据的 presentation quality。\n1073\t\n1074\t    '\n1075\t  tables: []\n1076\t  figures_description: []\n1077\t  analysis: 'P2 实验在 worst-tier 下应果断放弃。论文不需要第三个 negative result 来说明 CIVO 是 environment-specific。\n1078\t\n1079\t    '\n1080\t- name: Full cross-environment summary table\n1081\t  plan_id: N/A (synthesis)\n1082\t  description: 综合所有环境的 CIVO 检测结果\n1083\t  expected_results:\n1084\t    environments_with_confirmed_civo: 1\n1085\t    walker_walk:\n1086\t      civo_confirmed: true\n1087\t      nve_gt_1_5x_sensitivity: 3/3 (100%)\n1088\t      collapse_rate: 1/2 to 2/3 seeds\n1089\t      full_sgs_nve: 1.0\n1090\t      mechanism: observation-decoder-driven gradient amplification\n1091\t    cheetah_run:\n1092\t      civo_confirmed: false\n1093\t      nve_gt_1_5x_sensitivity: 0/3 (0%)\n1094\t      collapse_rate: 0/3\n1095\t      degradation: yes (-52% baseline)\n1096\t      mechanism: learning signal reduction + mild fidelity gap, no positive feedback\n1097\t        loop\n1098\t    cartpole_swingup:\n1099\t      civo_confirmed: false\n1100\t      nve_gt_1_5x_sensitivity: 0/3 (0%)\n1101\t      collapse_rate: 0/3\n1102\t      degradation: yes (-62% baseline)\n1103\t      mechanism: value suppression from sparse reward + dt>1 prediction noise\n1104\t    cross_env_threshold_accuracy: 0.65\n1105\t  result_rationale: 'Worst-tier 的 defining outcome：只有 Walker Walk 确认 CIVO。Cheetah\n1106\t    和 Cartpole 都显示 dt>1 degradation 但通过不同机制。1.5x NVE threshold 在 Walker 内完美 但跨环境仅\n1107\t    0.65 accuracy。这迫使论文完全退守 single-environment depth story。 贡献变为：(1) Walker Walk 的\n1108\t    rigorous factorial diagnosis，(2) NVE methodology （validated in Walker, proposed\n1109\t    with caveats），(3) gradient-level evidence （Full-SGS），(4) TAWM contrast（MPC vs\n1110\t    imagination）。 Drop 所有 \"general architectural vulnerability\" 语言。 Add extensive\n1111\t    limitations section 讨论 environment-specificity。\n1112\t\n1113\t    '\n1114\t  tables:\n1115\t  - title: Cross-environment CIVO summary\n1116\t    headers:\n1117\t    - Environment\n1118\t    - Degradation?\n1119\t    - CIVO (NVE>1.5x)?\n1120\t    - Collapse?\n1121\t    - Mechanism\n1122\t    rows:\n1123\t    - - Walker Walk\n1124\t      - Yes (-5% to -85%)\n1125\t      - Yes (3/3 seeds)\n1126\t      - Yes (1-2/3)\n1127\t      - CIVO + Pathway B\n1128\t    - - Cheetah Run\n1129\t      - Yes (-52%)\n1130\t      - No (0/3 seeds)\n1131\t      - No (0/3)\n1132\t      - Learning signal + fidelity gap\n1133\t    - - Cartpole Swingup\n1134\t      - Yes (-62%)\n1135\t      - No (0/3 seeds)\n1136\t      - No (0/3)\n1137\t      - Value suppression\n1138\t  figures_description:\n1139\t  - 'Cross-env NVE distribution violin plot: Walker (wide, right-skewed >1.5x) vs\n1140\t    Cheetah/Cartpole (narrow, centered <1.0x)'\n1141\t  analysis: '论文 framing 最终版： \"We provide the first rigorous factorial diagnosis of\n1142\t    why temporal abstraction fails in DreamerV3''s imagination-based training, demonstrated\n1143\t    in Walker Walk with controlled design. The CIVO mechanism — trained dt-embedding\n1144\t    amplifying RSSM fidelity gaps into value overestimation through observation decoder\n1145\t    gradients — is confirmed by gradient-level intervention (Full-SGS). Our NVE diagnostic\n1146\t    methodology achieves perfect separation in Walker Walk but does not generalize\n1147\t    to Cheetah Run or Cartpole Swingup, where degradation proceeds through different\n1148\t    mechanisms. This environment-specificity itself is an important finding: temporal\n1149\t    abstraction fails universally in our experiments, but the failure mode is environment-dependent,\n1150\t    complicating one-size-fits-all solutions. The contrast with TAWM (Nhu et al.,\n1151\t    ICML 2025), where dt-conditioning succeeds in MPC but fails in imagination, remains\n1152\t    the paper''s strongest novelty claim regardless of cross-environment generalization.\"'\n1153\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1b0edaaf-f3d3-4d02-90e4-a445b4dd87c2","uuid":"577edc3a-051f-4e48-b9da-d897006837dc","timestamp":"2026-05-16T14:26:04.230Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_9/projects/event-gated-adaptive-horizon/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260516T133210/worst/review_context.yaml","content":"narrative_guidance: 'Cheetah 未能干净复现 CIVO 模式（NVE 停留在 0.8-1.4x，无加速性过估计签名），Cartpole/ManiSkill3\n  亦无清晰 CIVO 信号。 论文退守为 Walker Walk 单环境深度机制研究。核心贡献重新定位为： (1) 首个严格析因诊断——在 DreamerV3 imagination-based\n  actor-critic 中揭示 temporal abstraction 失败的 specific causal chain； (2) NVE 诊断方法论（Walker\n  内 4/4 完美分类，提议更广泛使用但承认跨环境泛化受限）； (3) gradient-level 因果证据（Full-SGS NVE 1.00x）证明失败是\n  observation-decoder-driven 而非 reward-driven——即便限于单环境亦非显然。 TAWM 对比成为 novelty 支柱：\"dt-conditioning\n  在 MPC 中成功（TAWM, ICML 2025）但在 imagination 中失败——我们提供首个机制解释。\" 跨环境泛化声明全部删除，替换为 extensive\n  limitations section 讨论 Cheetah/Cartpole 为何动力学不同 （reward density、state dimensionality、RSSM\n  fidelity characteristics）。 仍可投 CoRL 作为 methodology + single-environment depth 论文，但接收概率下降；需\n  exceptional writing quality 和 TAWM contrast 支撑 novelty。\n\n  '\nimagined_experiments:\n- name: Walker Walk 008d (trained dt_emb, collapse) seeds 1-2\n  plan_id: plan_011\n  description: 复现 CIVO collapse，2 additional seeds\n  expected_results:\n    seed1_009e_final_eval: 131.08\n    seed1_009e_peak_nve: 4.12\n    seed1_009e_collapse: true\n    seed2_009b_final_eval: 267.93\n    seed2_009b_peak_nve: 2.05\n    seed2_009b_collapse: false\n    collapse_rate: 1/2 (50%)\n    nve_gt_1_5x_rate: 2/2 (100%)\n  result_rationale: '实际数据已收集。worst-tier 解读：collapse rate 仅 50%（1/2 独立 seed 崩溃）， 削弱\n    \"CIVO 是 deterministic failure\" 的叙事。009b 的自修正（NVE 2.05x@25K → 0.38x@105K） 证明 CIVO\n    反馈环并非不可逆——早期训练随机性决定路径分叉。这迫使论文用语从 \"trained dt_emb causes collapse\" 改为 \"trained\n    dt_emb reliably triggers pathological overestimation (NVE>1.5x), with collapse\n    as a stochastic consequence\"。 当 Cheetah 无法复现该模式时，50% collapse rate 的统计力量进一步被质疑。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: 008d config cross-seed comparison\n    headers:\n    - Metric\n    - Seed 0 (008d)\n    - Seed 1 (009e)\n    - Seed 2 (009b)\n    rows:\n    - - Peak NVE (35K+)\n      - 2.09x@45K\n      - 4.12x@55K\n      - 1.62x@45K\n    - - Collapse?\n      - Yes@55K\n      - Yes@55K\n      - No (self-correct)\n    - - Final eval@105K\n      - 82.7 (55K stop)\n      - '131.1'\n      - '267.9'\n    - - NVE trajectory\n      - accelerating\n      - accelerating\n      - transient peak → decline\n  figures_description:\n  - NVE 轨迹对比图：seed 0/1 加速发散 vs seed 2 自修正。标注 1.5x threshold 和 35K cutoff\n  analysis: 'Walker 内 NVE>1.5x diagnostic 仍有 2/2 sensitivity（trained seeds 全部 exceed），\n    但 collapse 的 stochastic nature 限制了 practical significance。当 Cheetah 数据加入 后（0/3\n    exceed 1.5x），threshold 的跨环境推广将失败。Worst-tier 下这组数据 退化为 Walker-specific 机制证据而非 general\n    vulnerability 证据。\n\n    '\n- name: Walker Walk 008f (dt_embed_dim=0) seeds 1-2\n  plan_id: plan_012\n  description: 复现因果控制稳定性，2 additional seeds\n  expected_results:\n    seed1_009f_status: killed (incomplete)\n    seed2_009c_final_eval: 148.34\n    seed2_009c_peak_nve: 1.26\n    seed2_009c_trend: peak 359@75K → decline to 148@105K\n    seed2_009c_collapse: false\n    protection_robust: false\n  result_rationale: '实际数据：009f 被 kill（无完整数据），009c 在 75K 后持续下降至 148（vs baseline 916，仅\n    16%）。 虽然 009c 的 NVE 始终 <1.5x（peak 1.26x@25K），符合 \"no CIVO\" 判定，但绝对性能极差。 Worst-tier\n    解读：dt_embed_dim=0 的 \"保护\" 极不 robust——seed 0 恢复到 503 而 seed 2 跌至 148。 保护机制是 seed-dependent\n    的，008f 不是可靠方案。因果方向（trained dt_emb → CIVO）仍成立 （两个 seed 均 NVE<1.5x），但 practical\n    value 有限。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: 008f config cross-seed\n    headers:\n    - Metric\n    - Seed 0 (008f)\n    - Seed 2 (009c)\n    rows:\n    - - Peak NVE\n      - 1.02x@25K\n      - 1.26x@25K\n    - - Final eval@105K\n      - '503'\n      - '148'\n    - - Recovery pattern\n      - Zigzag → 503\n      - Peak 359@75K → decline\n    - - vs baseline\n      - -45%\n      - -84%\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: '009c 的衰退说明去掉 dt_embedding 虽阻止 CIVO 但不保证学习成功——reward prediction 退化（MAE\n    75x baseline）本身就是严重代价。Worst-tier 下，这组数据用于因果论证 但不支持任何 practical recommendation。\n\n    '\n- name: Walker Walk 008e_v3 (dt=1 imag) seeds 1-2\n  plan_id: plan_014\n  description: C6 mitigation multi-seed validation\n  expected_results:\n    seed1_eval_105K: 869.9\n    seed1_nve_105K: 0.8\n    seed1_collapse: false\n    seed2_eval_105K: 137.0\n    seed2_nve_105K: 3.78\n    seed2_collapse: true\n    seed2_collapse_mechanism: non-CIVO (eval-driven, entropy ↑)\n    collapse_rate: 1/2 (50%)\n    c6_status: PARTIALLY FALSIFIED\n  result_rationale: '实际数据。s1 成功（95% baseline），s2 在 85-105K 崩溃（715→452→137），但机制与 经典\n    CIVO 不同：s2 是 eval-driven（eval 先跌，value 稳定，entropy ↑），而 008d 是 value-driven（value\n    爆炸，eval 后跌，entropy ↓）。009a baseline s2 在同期完全稳定 （618→596→836），排除 seed 脆弱性。Worst-tier\n    解读：dt=1 imagination 未降低 collapse rate（与 dt=2 同为 50%），C6 mitigation 被 falsify。Trained\n    dt_embedding 通过 Pathway B（non-CIVO policy instability）绕过 dt=1 保护。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: 008e_v3 Pathway A vs Pathway B\n    headers:\n    - Feature\n    - '008d s0 (Pathway A: CIVO)'\n    - '008e_v3 s2 (Pathway B: non-CIVO)'\n    rows:\n    - - Value change\n      - +130% explosion\n      - +13% stable\n    - - Eval change\n      - 后跌 -43%\n      - 先跌 -81%\n    - - NVE driver\n      - Value 分子驱动\n      - Eval 分母驱动\n    - - Actor entropy\n      - ↓ (-3.47→-4.88)\n      - ↑ (-5.21→-3.83)\n    - - Mechanism\n      - Critic overestimate → actor exploit\n      - Eval crash → value lag\n  figures_description:\n  - 双 pathway 对比图：value/eval/entropy 三轨并列，008d s0 vs 008e_v3 s2\n  analysis: 'C6 partially falsified 是 worst-tier 最关键的负面结果。论文需重新定位 trained dt_embedding\n    为 \"multi-pathway vulnerability creator\"，而非仅 CIVO trigger。但 Pathway B 机制 尚不充分理解——如果\n    plan_016 显示仅 1/4 崩溃，Pathway B 可能退化为 seed variance。\n\n    '\n- name: Walker Walk FROZEN dt_emb + subsample ON + dt=2 imag\n  plan_id: plan_015\n  description: 诊断 dt_emb TRAINING 是否为 CIVO 必要条件\n  expected_results:\n    final_eval_105K: 204.2\n    nve_range: 0.39-0.47\n    collapse: false\n    collapse_mechanism: gradient starvation (actor_loss→0)\n    gate_dt_mean: 2.0\n    actor_loss_105K: 0.000179\n  result_rationale: '实际数据（exp_015b）。Frozen dt_emb 导致 gradient starvation：随机初始化的 dt_embedding\n    不训练，为 RSSM 提供无信息 conditioning→critic 系统性低估（NVE 0.39-0.47x）， actor loss 趋近零，学习停滞。eval\n    在 80-238 间剧烈波动，无稳定收敛。 Worst-tier 解读：确认了一个消融点（frozen ≠ trained ≠ absent），但引入新失败模式\n    （gradient starvation），不能作为 mitigation。论文仅能作为 mechanism isolation 证据： dt_emb 的\n    training 过程本身驱动 CIVO。\n\n    '\n  tables: []\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: 'Frozen dt_emb 的 gradient starvation 是 worst-tier 下的一个 \"ugly control\"——\n    它证明了 dt_emb training 是 CIVO 必要条件，但方式不够 clean（引入新问题而非 neutral baseline）。论文中需小心呈现：这是析因矩阵中的一个消融点，而非独立\n    finding。\n\n    '\n- name: Walker Walk 008a (untrained dt_emb, V-recovery) seeds 1-2\n  plan_id: plan_013\n  description: 复现 value growth suppression，2 additional seeds\n  expected_results:\n    seed1_eval_trajectory:\n      35K: 460\n      45K: 510\n      55K: 440\n      65K: 550\n      75K: 480\n      85K: 530\n      95K: 520\n      105K: 700\n    seed1_nve_range_55K_105K:\n    - 0.6\n    - 0.85\n    seed1_final_eval: 700\n    seed1_vs_baseline_105K: -23.5%\n    seed2_eval_trajectory:\n      35K: 420\n      45K: 480\n      55K: 400\n      65K: 470\n      75K: 430\n      85K: 510\n      95K: 490\n      105K: 620\n    seed2_nve_range_55K_105K:\n    - 0.55\n    - 0.8\n    seed2_final_eval: 620\n    seed2_vs_baseline_105K: -32.3%\n    cross_seed_mean_105K: 699\n    cross_seed_nve_mean_105K: 0.63\n  result_rationale: 'Worst-tier 下 C3 在 Walker 内仍 hold，但 variance 更大。Seed 0 (778@105K,\n    85% baseline) 是最优 seed；seed 1-2 预计较低（700/620@105K，76%/68% baseline），因为 subsample\n    OFF + untrained dt_emb 的保护性依赖 RSSM 在 dt=1 数据上的收敛质量——不同 seed 的 RSSM 初始化影响 dt=1\n    prediction 精度，进而影响 value calibration。Normalized v/e 仍一致 低于 1.0x（无 CIVO），但绝对性能比\n    seed 0 差，拉低 cross-seed IQM。 在 worst-tier 下这不影响 C3 的定性结论，但 Agarwal et al. (2021)\n    IQM + CI 会更宽。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: 008a cross-seed summary\n    headers:\n    - Metric\n    - Seed 0\n    - Seed 1 (pred)\n    - Seed 2 (pred)\n    - Mean\n    rows:\n    - - Eval@105K\n      - '778'\n      - '700'\n      - '620'\n      - '699'\n    - - vs baseline\n      - -15%\n      - -24%\n      - -32%\n      - -24%\n    - - NVE@105K\n      - 0.59x\n      - 0.65x\n      - 0.72x\n      - 0.65x\n    - - Collapse?\n      - 'No'\n      - 'No'\n      - 'No'\n      - 0/3\n  figures_description:\n  - 三 seed 学习曲线叠加，均显示 zigzag 但幅度和收敛点不同\n  analysis: 'C3 在 Walker 内 robust（3/3 seeds NVE<1.0x，无崩溃），但跨 seed 绝对性能变化大 （620-778，22%\n    跨距）。Worst-tier 下，这组数据仅 reinforces Walker-specific 结论。\n\n    '\n- name: Walker Walk 008e_v3 additional seeds (seed 3-4)\n  plan_id: plan_016\n  description: 缩窄 Pathway B collapse probability estimate\n  expected_results:\n    seed3_eval_105K: 830\n    seed3_nve_105K: 0.78\n    seed3_collapse: false\n    seed4_eval_105K: 790\n    seed4_nve_105K: 0.82\n    seed4_collapse: false\n    total_collapse_rate: 1/4 (25%)\n    pathway_b_interpretation: closer to seed variance than systematic pathway\n  result_rationale: 'Worst-tier 核心假设之一：\"Pathway B control experiment reveals 008e_v3_s2\n    collapse was closer to random seed variance than a systematic second pathway\"。Seed\n    3-4 均不崩溃，collapse rate 从 1/2 降至 1/4（25%）。在 4 个 seed 中仅 1 个崩溃， 且该崩溃的机制签名（entropy\n    ↑, eval-driven）与 CIVO 不同，更接近 policy optimization 的随机脆弱性。这削弱 \"multiple vulnerability\n    pathways\" 叙事—— Pathway B 不是 systematic mechanism 而是 seed-specific instability。\n    论文需要 honest reporting：trained dt_emb + dt=1 imag 的 collapse rate ~25%， 无法确定是否显著高于\n    baseline（baseline 0/2 seeds 崩溃，但 n 太小无法做统计检验）。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: 008e_v3 all seeds\n    headers:\n    - Seed\n    - Eval@105K\n    - NVE@105K\n    - Collapse?\n    - Mechanism\n    rows:\n    - - Seed 1 (s1)\n      - '869.9'\n      - 0.80x\n      - 'No'\n      - '-'\n    - - Seed 2 (s2)\n      - '137.0'\n      - 3.78x\n      - 'Yes'\n      - Eval-driven (Pathway B)\n    - - Seed 3 (pred)\n      - '830'\n      - 0.78x\n      - 'No'\n      - '-'\n    - - Seed 4 (pred)\n      - '790'\n      - 0.82x\n      - 'No'\n      - '-'\n  figures_description:\n  - 4-seed 学习曲线 + NVE 轨迹，标注 seed 2 崩溃点及与其余 3 seeds 的分歧\n  analysis: '1/4 collapse rate 在 worst-tier 下严重削弱 Pathway B 论述。论文可能需要从 \"trained dt_embedding\n    creates vulnerability through multiple pathways\" 退回到 \"trained dt_embedding reliably\n    triggers CIVO (Pathway A, blocked by dt=1 imag); rare policy instability events\n    (1/4 seeds) may or may not be related\"。 这实际上部分 salvages dt=1 mitigation（3/4 seeds\n    成功，接近 baseline）， 但 honest reporting 要求承认 n=4 统计力量不足。\n\n    '\n- name: NVE threshold sensitivity analysis\n  plan_id: plan_034\n  description: 不同 NVE 阈值的分类精度，0 GPU 成本\n  expected_results:\n    walker_only:\n      threshold_1_3x:\n        accuracy: 0.8\n        sensitivity: 1.0\n        specificity: 0.5\n        note: 1 FP (009c@25K NVE=1.26 borderline, 但 35K+ 限定后为 TN)\n      threshold_1_5x:\n        accuracy: 1.0\n        sensitivity: 1.0\n        specificity: 1.0\n        note: 4/4 perfect at 35K+\n      threshold_1_7x:\n        accuracy: 0.8\n        sensitivity: 0.67\n        specificity: 1.0\n        note: 009b peak NVE=1.62x barely above 1.7x? Actually no, 1.62<1.7 → FN\n      threshold_2_0x:\n        accuracy: 0.8\n        sensitivity: 0.67\n        specificity: 1.0\n        note: 009b peak 2.05x@25K excluded by 35K+ rule; 1.62x@45K<2.0 → FN\n      auroc: 0.98\n    cross_env_walker_cheetah:\n      threshold_1_5x:\n        accuracy: 0.64\n        sensitivity: 0.4\n        specificity: 1.0\n        note: Walker 2/2 trained→TP; Cheetah 0/3 trained→FN; all untrained→TN\n      auroc: 0.72\n    cross_env_all_three:\n      threshold_1_5x:\n        accuracy: 0.58\n        sensitivity: 0.29\n        specificity: 1.0\n        note: 仅 Walker 2/7 trained seeds 被检出\n      auroc: 0.65\n  result_rationale: 'Walker 内 1.5x threshold 完美分离（AUROC~0.98），这是 existing data 的强结论。\n    但在 worst-tier 下，Cheetah 的 trained dt_emb seeds NVE 全部 <1.5x（范围 0.8-1.4x）， 因为 Cheetah\n    的 RSSM fidelity characteristics 不同——reward density 更高、state dynamics 更 smooth，dt_emb\n    的 observation decoder 梯度不产生同样的 systematic bias。 这导致 threshold 在 Cheetah 上产生大量\n    false negatives（degradation 发生但 NVE 不超标）。Cross-env AUROC 从 0.98 降至 ~0.72，远低于 diagnostic\n    tool 的实用标准。 论文必须 honest report：\"NVE>1.5x is a reliable Walker Walk diagnostic\n    but does NOT generalize to Cheetah Run, where degradation manifests through different\n    dynamics.\"\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: NVE 1.5x threshold cross-environment performance\n    headers:\n    - Environment\n    - Trained Seeds\n    - TP\n    - FN\n    - Untrained Seeds\n    - TN\n    - FP\n    - Accuracy\n    rows:\n    - - Walker Walk\n      - '3'\n      - '3'\n      - '0'\n      - '2'\n      - '2'\n      - '0'\n      - 5/5=1.00\n    - - Cheetah Run\n      - '3'\n      - '0'\n      - '3'\n      - '3'\n      - '3'\n      - '0'\n      - 3/6=0.50\n    - - Cartpole Swingup\n      - '3'\n      - '0'\n      - '3'\n      - '3'\n      - '3'\n      - '0'\n      - 3/6=0.50\n    - - Cross-env total\n      - '9'\n      - '3'\n      - '6'\n      - '8'\n      - '8'\n      - '0'\n      - 11/17=0.65\n  figures_description:\n  - ROC 曲线：Walker-only (AUROC=0.98) vs cross-env (AUROC=0.72)\n  analysis: 'NVE 方法论是 worst-tier 下论文的 second contribution pillar，但必须诚实定位为 \"validated\n    in Walker Walk, proposed for broader adoption with caveats\"。跨环境失败 不否定方法论本身——而是揭示\n    CIVO 机制的 environment-specificity。论文应讨论 为何 Cheetah 的 NVE pattern 不同（reward density、RSSM\n    fidelity characteristics）， 将 negative result 转化为 diagnostic insight。\n\n    '\n- name: Cheetah Run baseline (3 seeds)\n  plan_id: plan_020\n  description: 第二 DMC 环境的 dt=1 baseline\n  expected_results:\n    seed1_final_eval: 849.8\n    seed1_status: DONE (exp_010a)\n    seed2_final_eval: 825\n    seed3_final_eval: 862\n    cross_seed_mean: 846\n    cross_seed_std: 19\n    ve_ratio_stable: 0.65-0.72 from 135K+\n    ve_ratio_trajectory:\n      25K: 0.09\n      35K: 0.19\n      45K: 0.28\n      55K: 0.36\n      65K: 0.47\n      75K: 0.57\n      85K: 0.63\n      95K: 0.66\n      105K: 0.68\n  result_rationale: 'Cheetah Run baseline 在 DreamerV3 上训练正常，peak ~850。Seed 1 已完成（849.8）。\n    Cheetah 的 reward 是 forward velocity（dense, smooth），收敛特性与 Walker Walk 类似 但 v/e\n    trajectory 略低（Cheetah 的 discount structure 和 reward scale 不同）。 Baseline 本身不受 worst-tier\n    影响——环境正常运行是所有后续实验的前提。\n\n    '\n  tables: []\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: 'Baseline 确立 Cheetah Run 的参考线。v/e calibration（~0.68@105K）与 Walker（~0.656@105K）\n    高度一致，为 NVE 比较提供合理基础。\n\n    '\n- name: Cheetah Run trained dt_emb + subsample ON (3 seeds)\n  plan_id: plan_021\n  description: 复现 CIVO collapse in Cheetah — worst-tier 预测失败\n  expected_results:\n    seed0:\n      eval_trajectory:\n        5K: 31\n        15K: 190\n        25K: 370\n        35K: 520\n        45K: 490\n        55K: 440\n        65K: 400\n        75K: 380\n        85K: 360\n        95K: 370\n        105K: 385\n      value_trajectory:\n        25K: 28\n        35K: 85\n        45K: 120\n        55K: 140\n        65K: 145\n        75K: 140\n        85K: 130\n        95K: 125\n        105K: 128\n      nve_trajectory:\n        35K: 0.94\n        45K: 0.92\n        55K: 0.95\n        65K: 0.83\n        75K: 0.72\n        85K: 0.68\n        95K: 0.65\n        105K: 0.63\n      collapse: false\n      peak_nve: 0.95\n      pattern: gradual decline without value acceleration\n    seed1:\n      eval_trajectory:\n        35K: 480\n        45K: 430\n        55K: 380\n        65K: 350\n        75K: 340\n        85K: 360\n        95K: 375\n        105K: 390\n      nve_trajectory:\n        35K: 1.25\n        45K: 1.3\n        55K: 1.28\n        65K: 1.15\n        75K: 0.98\n        85K: 0.92\n        95K: 0.88\n        105K: 0.85\n      collapse: false\n      peak_nve: 1.3\n      pattern: mild overestimation plateau then decline — not accelerating\n    seed2:\n      eval_trajectory:\n        35K: 550\n        45K: 520\n        55K: 470\n        65K: 430\n        75K: 410\n        85K: 420\n        95K: 430\n        105K: 445\n      nve_trajectory:\n        35K: 0.82\n        45K: 0.85\n        55K: 0.9\n        65K: 0.87\n        75K: 0.8\n        85K: 0.78\n        95K: 0.75\n        105K: 0.74\n      collapse: false\n      peak_nve: 0.9\n      pattern: value suppression — similar to Walker dt=4\n    cross_seed_collapse_rate: 0/3\n    cross_seed_nve_max: 1.3\n    cross_seed_nve_mean_at_55K: 1.04\n    cross_seed_eval_mean_105K: 407\n    vs_baseline_105K: -52%\n  result_rationale: \"Worst-tier 核心假设：\\\"Cheetah Run shows performance degradation with\\\n    \\ dt>1 but NVE pattern differs\\\"。三个 seed 均显示 degradation（eval 407 平均 vs baseline\\\n    \\ 846，-52%），但 NVE 模式与 Walker 定性不同： (1) Seed 0 (NVE 0.63-0.95x)：value suppression\\\n    \\ 模式，类似 Walker dt=4——RSSM 在\\n    Cheetah 的 dt>1 prediction 质量差导致 critic underestimate\\\n    \\ 而非 overestimate。\\n    Cheetah 的 velocity-based reward 结构使 dt>1 reward prediction\\\n    \\ 偏差方向不同。\\n(2) Seed 1 (NVE peak 1.30x)：温和过估计但不加速。NVE 在 35-55K 达到 1.25-1.30x\\n\\\n    \\    后自行下降至 0.85x。与 Walker 008d 的加速发散（1.71x→2.09x→4.12x）形成鲜明对比。\\n    Cheetah 的\\\n    \\ RSSM 可能在 dt>1 有更好的 self-correction 能力（state space 更规则）。\\n(3) Seed 2 (NVE 0.74-0.90x)：纯\\\n    \\ value suppression。 没有任何 seed 的 NVE 超过 1.5x → 1.5x threshold 在 Cheetah 上完全失效（0/3\\\n    \\ detected）。 Degradation 确实存在但不是 CIVO——更可能是 learning signal reduction (C5) + RSSM\\\n    \\ fidelity gap 的混合效应，不伴随 positive feedback loop。\\n\"\n  tables:\n  - title: Cheetah CIVO trigger cross-seed NVE\n    headers:\n    - Step\n    - Seed 0 NVE\n    - Seed 1 NVE\n    - Seed 2 NVE\n    - Walker 008d NVE (ref)\n    rows:\n    - - 35K\n      - '0.94'\n      - '1.25'\n      - '0.82'\n      - '1.71'\n    - - 45K\n      - '0.92'\n      - '1.30'\n      - '0.85'\n      - '2.09'\n    - - 55K\n      - '0.95'\n      - '1.28'\n      - '0.90'\n      - '4.12'\n    - - 65K\n      - '0.83'\n      - '1.15'\n      - '0.87'\n      - (collapsed)\n    - - 105K\n      - '0.63'\n      - '0.85'\n      - '0.74'\n      - '-'\n  figures_description:\n  - Cheetah vs Walker NVE 轨迹对比：Walker 加速发散 vs Cheetah 平稳/下降\n  - Cheetah 3-seed eval 曲线 + baseline reference\n  analysis: '这是 worst-tier 的 defining result。Degradation 存在但 CIVO 缺失。论文必须承认： \"The\n    CIVO mechanism (accelerating NVE feedback loop) is environment-specific. In Cheetah\n    Run, trained dt_embedding degrades performance through a different mechanism —\n    likely learning signal quality degradation without the positive feedback loop\n    observed in Walker.\" Limitations section 需讨论 Cheetah 为何不同：(a) reward 结构（pure velocity\n    vs complex locomotion reward），(b) state space dimensionality 和 smoothness， (c)\n    RSSM 对不同 dynamics 的 fidelity characteristics。\n\n    '\n- name: Cheetah Run dt_embed_dim=0 + subsample ON (3 seeds)\n  plan_id: plan_022\n  description: Cheetah 因果控制——worst-tier 预测无 clean separation\n  expected_results:\n    seed0:\n      eval_trajectory:\n        35K: 470\n        55K: 400\n        75K: 370\n        105K: 410\n      nve_trajectory:\n        35K: 0.75\n        55K: 0.9\n        75K: 0.85\n        105K: 0.7\n      pattern: similar degradation to trained dt_emb\n    seed1:\n      eval_trajectory:\n        35K: 510\n        55K: 430\n        75K: 400\n        105K: 440\n      nve_trajectory:\n        35K: 0.68\n        55K: 0.8\n        75K: 0.75\n        105K: 0.65\n    seed2:\n      eval_trajectory:\n        35K: 490\n        55K: 420\n        75K: 380\n        105K: 380\n      nve_trajectory:\n        35K: 1.1\n        55K: 1.05\n        75K: 0.9\n        105K: 0.82\n    cross_seed_eval_mean_105K: 410\n    cross_seed_nve_range:\n    - 0.65\n    - 1.1\n    nve_overlap_with_trained: substantial (trained range [0.63, 1.30] vs untrained\n      [0.65, 1.10])\n    vs_trained_dt_emb_eval_diff: +0.7% (not significant)\n  result_rationale: 'Worst-tier 假设：\"NVE 1.5x threshold doesn''t separate trained/untrained\n    in Cheetah\"。 去掉 dt_embedding 后 Cheetah 的 eval 和 NVE 与 trained dt_emb 配置几乎无差异 （eval\n    410 vs 407, NVE 0.65-1.10 vs 0.63-1.30）。原因：Cheetah 的 degradation 根源是 learning\n    signal reduction（subsample ON 导致有效 transition 数减半）而非 dt_embedding-driven CIVO。在\n    Walker 中，去掉 dt_emb 阻止了 CIVO feedback loop， 产生 dramatic 差异（008f NVE<1.0 vs 008d\n    NVE>2.0）；在 Cheetah 中，没有 CIVO feedback loop 需要阻止，所以去掉 dt_emb 不产生 significant effect。\n    这是 worst-tier 下最难处理的结果——直接否定 C2 因果链在 Cheetah 上的适用性。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: 'Cheetah: trained vs no dt_emb'\n    headers:\n    - Metric\n    - Trained dt_emb (plan_021)\n    - No dt_emb (plan_022)\n    - Δ\n    rows:\n    - - Eval mean@105K\n      - '407'\n      - '410'\n      - +0.7% (ns)\n    - - NVE range (35K+)\n      - '[0.63, 1.30]'\n      - '[0.65, 1.10]'\n      - overlapping\n    - - Collapse rate\n      - 0/3\n      - 0/3\n      - identical\n    - - NVE>1.5x rate\n      - 0/3\n      - 0/3\n      - identical\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Cheetah trained vs untrained dt_emb: eval + NVE 并排对比，标注 overlap region'\n  analysis: 'Cheetah 的 \"no separation\" 是 worst-tier 最 damaging 的 cross-env negative\n    result。 论文需要解释为什么 Walker 的因果机制不 transfer：dt_embedding 在 Cheetah 的 observation\n    decoder 梯度路径可能不产生同向 systematic bias，因为 Cheetah 的 state space structure（关节速度为主导\n    observable）让 RSSM 对 dt>1 的 prediction error 分布更 uniform（不集中在特定 decoder head），无法形成\n    amplification loop。\n\n    '\n- name: Cheetah Run untrained dt_emb + no subsample (3 seeds)\n  plan_id: plan_023\n  description: Cheetah value growth suppression — worst-tier 预测无 clear advantage\n  expected_results:\n    seed0:\n      eval_trajectory:\n        35K: 490\n        55K: 430\n        75K: 450\n        105K: 520\n      nve_trajectory:\n        35K: 0.8\n        55K: 0.75\n        75K: 0.7\n        105K: 0.65\n    seed1:\n      eval_trajectory:\n        35K: 520\n        55K: 460\n        75K: 480\n        105K: 550\n      nve_trajectory:\n        35K: 0.72\n        55K: 0.78\n        75K: 0.68\n        105K: 0.6\n    seed2:\n      eval_trajectory:\n        35K: 480\n        55K: 440\n        75K: 430\n        105K: 490\n      nve_trajectory:\n        35K: 0.85\n        55K: 0.82\n        75K: 0.75\n        105K: 0.7\n    cross_seed_eval_mean_105K: 520\n    vs_baseline: -39%\n    vs_trained_dt_emb: +28% (520 vs 407)\n    vs_no_dt_emb: +27% (520 vs 410)\n  result_rationale: 'Subsample OFF 保留完整 learning signal，所以 eval 高于 plan_021/022（520\n    vs 407/410）。 但这个提升来自 learning signal preservation（C5），不是 value suppression（C3）。\n    NVE 在 0.60-0.85x 范围，与 plan_022 (0.65-1.10) 有 overlap。Worst-tier 解读： C3 在 Cheetah\n    上不能 cleanly 验证，因为 baseline comparison 被 subsample 差异混淆。 To isolate C3 需要 subsample\n    ON + untrained dt_emb（但 Walker 已有 008c/008e_v3 数据做此对比）。在 Cheetah 上，所有 dt>1 配置都\n    degrades，无论 dt_emb 状态如何。\n\n    '\n  tables: []\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: 'Cheetah untrained dt_emb 的 eval 提升主要归因于 subsample OFF（保留学习信号）， 非 value\n    suppression 机制。C3 声明在 Cheetah 上 confounded。\n\n    '\n- name: Cartpole Swingup baseline (3 seeds)\n  plan_id: plan_050\n  description: 非 locomotion 环境 baseline\n  expected_results:\n    seed0_final_eval: 840\n    seed1_final_eval: 820\n    seed2_final_eval: 855\n    cross_seed_mean: 838\n    ve_ratio_stable: 0.60-0.68 from 135K+\n  result_rationale: 'Cartpole Swingup 是 DreamerV3 上的 well-solved benchmark，baseline\n    ~840。 V/e ratio 收敛到 ~0.64，略低于 Walker/Cheetah，因为 Cartpole 的 sparse initial reward（swingup\n    前 reward 极低）使 value function 在 early training 更保守。\n\n    '\n  tables: []\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: 'Baseline 正常。Cartpole 的 non-locomotion dynamics（pendulum + cart） 为跨环境泛化测试提供了不同\n    task family。\n\n    '\n- name: Cartpole Swingup trained dt_emb + subsample ON (3 seeds)\n  plan_id: plan_051\n  description: 复现 CIVO collapse in Cartpole — worst-tier 预测 no CIVO\n  expected_results:\n    seed0:\n      eval_105K: 320\n      peak_nve: 0.75\n      pattern: value suppression — critic under-estimates\n    seed1:\n      eval_105K: 280\n      peak_nve: 0.9\n      pattern: learning failure — low asymptote\n    seed2:\n      eval_105K: 350\n      peak_nve: 0.65\n      pattern: value suppression\n    cross_seed_eval_mean: 317\n    vs_baseline: -62%\n    collapse_rate: 0/3\n    nve_max: 0.9\n    nve_gt_1_5x: 0/3\n  result_rationale: \"Cartpole Swingup 的 sparse reward structure 使 dt>1 transitions\\\n    \\ 的 reward prediction 几乎无信息（swingup 前大量 near-zero reward）。Trained dt_emb 不会产生\\\n    \\ CIVO 因为： (1) RSSM 对 dt>1 的 reward prediction 偏差方向是 under-estimation（sparse reward\\n\\\n    \\    的高 reward events 在 dt>1 步后更难预测，导致 systematic negative bias）；\\n(2) Observation\\\n    \\ decoder 梯度集中在 pendulum angle 上（单一关键 observable），\\n    不像 Walker 的 multi-head\\\n    \\ gradient（orientations/velocity/height）能形成\\n    amplification；\\n(3) Cartpole\\\n    \\ 的 state space（4D: cart pos/vel + pole angle/vel）远小于\\n    Walker（24D+），RSSM 的\\\n    \\ dt>1 fidelity gap 更小。\\n结果是 degradation 但以 value suppression/learning failure\\\n    \\ 形式出现，无 CIVO signature。\\n\"\n  tables:\n  - title: Cartpole trained dt_emb NVE\n    headers:\n    - Seed\n    - Peak NVE\n    - NVE@105K\n    - Collapse?\n    - Pattern\n    rows:\n    - - '0'\n      - '0.75'\n      - '0.60'\n      - 'No'\n      - Value suppression\n    - - '1'\n      - '0.90'\n      - '0.70'\n      - 'No'\n      - Learning failure\n    - - '2'\n      - '0.65'\n      - '0.55'\n      - 'No'\n      - Value suppression\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: 'Cartpole 的 NVE pattern（全部 <1.0x）与 Walker 的 CIVO（>1.5x accelerating）和\n    Cheetah 的 mixed pattern（0.6-1.3x stable）都不同。三个环境三种 failure mode： Walker=CIVO,\n    Cheetah=mild overestimation/plateau, Cartpole=value suppression。 这证明 dt>1 degradation\n    是 universal 但 mechanism 是 environment-specific。\n\n    '\n- name: Cartpole Swingup dt_embed_dim=0 + subsample ON (3 seeds)\n  plan_id: plan_052\n  description: Cartpole 因果控制\n  expected_results:\n    seed0_eval_105K: 310\n    seed1_eval_105K: 290\n    seed2_eval_105K: 340\n    cross_seed_eval_mean: 313\n    vs_trained_dt_emb: -1.3% (not significant)\n    nve_range:\n    - 0.55\n    - 0.85\n    nve_overlap_with_trained: complete overlap\n  result_rationale: '与 Cheetah 类似，去掉 dt_embedding 在 Cartpole 上不产生 significant 差异。\n    Degradation 根源是 learning signal reduction（C5），dt_emb 不是 primary factor。 Eval 313\n    vs trained 317，差异在噪声范围内。NVE 完全 overlap。 Walker 中 008f vs 008d 的 dramatic 差异（NVE\n    0.97x vs 2.09x）在 Cartpole 不可复现——因为 Cartpole 没有 CIVO feedback loop 需要 dt_emb 来\n    trigger。\n\n    '\n  tables: []\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: 'Cartpole 的 \"no separation\" 进一步确认：CIVO 是 Walker-specific phenomenon。 Cross-env\n    data 现在显示 3 environments 中仅 1 个有 CIVO。\n\n    '\n- name: 'RSSM prediction quality: dt=1 vs dt=2 transitions'\n  plan_id: plan_030\n  description: 量化 RSSM fidelity gap 的 environment-specific characteristics\n  expected_results:\n    cheetah_baseline:\n      dt1_obs_mse: 10.2\n      dt2_obs_mse: 18.5\n      obs_gap: 1.81\n      dt1_reward_mae: 0.008\n      dt2_reward_mae: 0.012\n      reward_gap: 1.5\n    cheetah_trained_dt_emb:\n      dt1_obs_mse: 15.8\n      dt2_obs_mse: 22.3\n      obs_gap: 1.41\n      dt1_reward_mae: 0.035\n      dt2_reward_mae: 0.065\n      reward_gap: 1.86\n    cheetah_no_dt_emb:\n      dt1_obs_mse: 9.5\n      dt2_obs_mse: 19.8\n      obs_gap: 2.08\n      dt1_reward_mae: 0.52\n      dt2_reward_mae: 0.54\n      reward_gap: 1.04\n    walker_vs_cheetah_obs_gap_comparison:\n      walker_baseline: 2.04\n      cheetah_baseline: 1.81\n      walker_trained: 1.3\n      cheetah_trained: 1.41\n  result_rationale: \"Cheetah 的 RSSM fidelity gap 与 Walker 数值接近但分布不同。关键差异： (1) Cheetah\\\n    \\ 的 trained dt_emb reward gap (1.86x) 低于 Walker (2.78x)——\\n    Cheetah 的 velocity\\\n    \\ reward 更 smooth，dt_emb 不会像 Walker 那样在 reward head\\n    产生 large systematic bias。但注意\\\n    \\ Walker 的 reward gradient = 0（by architecture），\\n    所以 reward gap 不是 CIVO 的直接驱动因素。\\n\\\n    (2) Cheetah 的 obs_gap (1.81x baseline, 1.41x trained) 与 Walker (2.04x, 1.30x)\\\n    \\ \\n    类似，但 obs MSE 的绝对值更低——Cheetah 的 state space 更规则，RSSM 建模质量更好。\\n(3) Cheetah\\\n    \\ trained dt_emb 的 dt1 abs obs_MSE (15.8) 显著低于 Walker (41.31)——\\n    模型没有像 Walker\\\n    \\ 那样因为 CIVO 而全面崩塌。\\nWorst-tier 解读：fidelity gap 存在但不 sufficient to trigger CIVO\\\n    \\ in Cheetah。 机制的 environment-specificity 体现在 fidelity gap 如何通过 gradient pathways\\\n    \\ 传播到 value function——Walker 的 multi-head gradient structure 放大 bias， Cheetah\\\n    \\ 的更 uniform gradient 不放大。\\n\"\n  tables:\n  - title: Cross-environment RSSM fidelity comparison\n    headers:\n    - Model\n    - Env\n    - dt1 obs_MSE\n    - dt2 obs_MSE\n    - obs gap\n    - reward gap\n    rows:\n    - - Baseline\n      - Walker\n      - '13.49'\n      - '27.50'\n      - 2.04x\n      - 1.56x\n    - - Baseline\n      - Cheetah\n      - '10.2'\n      - '18.5'\n      - 1.81x\n      - 1.50x\n    - - Trained dt_emb\n      - Walker\n      - '41.31'\n      - '53.67'\n      - 1.30x\n      - 2.78x\n    - - Trained dt_emb\n      - Cheetah\n      - '15.8'\n      - '22.3'\n      - 1.41x\n      - 1.86x\n    - - No dt_emb\n      - Walker\n      - '8.01'\n      - '22.04'\n      - 2.75x\n      - 1.01x\n    - - No dt_emb\n      - Cheetah\n      - '9.5'\n      - '19.8'\n      - 2.08x\n      - 1.04x\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Cross-env RSSM fidelity heatmap: obs_MSE × reward_MAE 四象限，标注 CIVO/non-CIVO regions'\n  analysis: 'RSSM fidelity gap 是 necessary but not sufficient for CIVO。Cheetah 有 gap\n    但 无 CIVO 放大。论文需讨论 gradient pathway structure 作为 missing mediator。\n\n    '\n- name: Actor entropy analysis\n  plan_id: plan_031\n  description: Walker + Cheetah actor entropy trajectory 对比\n  expected_results:\n    walker_civo_collapsed_008d:\n      entropy_trajectory: 8.2→-1.9→-3.5→-4.6→-4.9\n      pattern: 'entropy ↓: policy becomes deterministic during CIVO'\n    walker_pathway_b_008e_v3_s2:\n      entropy_trajectory: -5.1→-5.2→-5.2→-4.5→-3.8\n      pattern: 'entropy ↑: policy destabilizes (opposite of CIVO)'\n    walker_healthy_008a:\n      entropy_trajectory: -4.2→-4.5→-4.6→-4.7→-4.8\n      pattern: 'entropy stable: normal policy convergence'\n    cheetah_trained_dt_emb:\n      entropy_trajectory: -3.8→-4.0→-4.1→-4.2→-4.3\n      pattern: 'entropy stable: no CIVO or Pathway B signature'\n    cheetah_no_dt_emb:\n      entropy_trajectory: -3.7→-3.9→-4.0→-4.1→-4.2\n      pattern: 'entropy stable: indistinguishable from trained'\n  result_rationale: 'Actor entropy 在 Walker 中是 CIVO 和 Pathway B 的 discriminating signature：\n    CIVO → entropy ↓（critic overestimate 让 actor converge to exploitative policy），\n    Pathway B → entropy ↑（policy destabilization，actor 失去 coherent strategy）。 在 Cheetah\n    中，因为没有 CIVO 或 Pathway B，所有配置的 entropy trajectory  几乎一致（stable decline），无法作为 diagnostic\n    tool。这进一步确认 Cheetah 的 degradation 机制不同——没有 actor 层面的 pathological dynamics。\n\n    '\n  tables: []\n  figures_description:\n  - Walker entropy 三轨对比（CIVO↓ / Pathway B↑ / healthy→）vs Cheetah 无差异\n  analysis: 'Entropy analysis 在 Walker 内是有力 diagnostic，但在 Cheetah 上无差异性。 论文可呈现为 Walker-specific\n    finding。\n\n    '\n- name: Value prediction distribution vs realized returns\n  plan_id: plan_032\n  description: V(s) vs MC return 分布分析\n  expected_results:\n    walker_008d_divergence:\n      value_mean: 97.5\n      mc_return_mean: 35\n      ks_statistic: 0.72\n      pattern: right-shifted value distribution — systematic overestimation\n    walker_008a_calibration:\n      value_mean: 280\n      mc_return_mean: 550\n      ks_statistic: 0.35\n      pattern: left-shifted but not pathological — conservative value\n    cheetah_trained_divergence:\n      value_mean: 140\n      mc_return_mean: 180\n      ks_statistic: 0.28\n      pattern: mild underestimation — no systematic overestimation\n  result_rationale: 'Walker 008d 的 V(s) 分布系统性右偏（overestimate），与 MC return 严重脱节 （KS=0.72）。这是\n    CIVO 的 direct evidence。Cheetah trained dt_emb 的 V(s) 分布仅轻微左偏（underestimate, KS=0.28），不存在\n    systematic overestimation。 Worst-tier 下，分布分析强化了 \"CIVO is Walker-specific\" 的结论。\n\n    '\n  tables: []\n  figures_description:\n  - 'V(s) vs MC return 散点图 + violin plot: Walker 008d (divergent) vs Cheetah (aligned)'\n  analysis: '分布分析是比 v/e ratio 更 informative 的 proxy，但在 worst-tier 下仅确认 已知结论。投入 1 GPU-hour\n    的 ROI 有限。\n\n    '\n- name: dt_embedding cosine similarity analysis\n  plan_id: plan_033\n  description: learned dt_emb vectors 的 dt=1 vs dt=2 similarity evolution\n  expected_results:\n    walker_initial_cosine: 0.85\n    walker_trained_30K_cosine: 0.42\n    walker_trained_60K_cosine: 0.28\n    walker_trend: diverging — dt=1 and dt=2 embeddings become increasingly dissimilar\n    cheetah_initial_cosine: 0.85\n    cheetah_trained_30K_cosine: 0.55\n    cheetah_trained_60K_cosine: 0.48\n    cheetah_trend: partial divergence — less separation than Walker\n  result_rationale: 'Walker 中 dt_emb 的 dt=1 和 dt=2 vectors 快速分化（cosine 0.85→0.28），\n    说明 network 积极利用 dt conditioning 来做 specialized predictions——这是 CIVO 的前提条件。Cheetah\n    中分化较缓（0.85→0.48），说明 dt_emb 被利用程度 较低——network 未充分 specialize on dt information，因此不会形成\n    strong dt-dependent value bias。这与 Cheetah 的 observation decoder 梯度更 uniform 的假设一致——没有足够的\n    gradient signal 来 push dt_emb 向 high-separation direction。\n\n    '\n  tables: []\n  figures_description:\n  - 'dt_emb cosine similarity vs training step: Walker (fast divergence) vs Cheetah\n    (slow)'\n  analysis: 'Cosine analysis 提供了为什么 CIVO 在 Cheetah 不发生的 additional mechanistic insight：\n    dt_embedding 在 Cheetah 中学到的 dt 区分度更低，减少了 condition-dependent bias 的 severity。可作为\n    Discussion section 的 supporting analysis。0 GPU cost，值得做。\n\n    '\n- name: Uncertainty-gated imagination truncation pilot\n  plan_id: plan_060\n  description: RSSM 不确定性门控 imagination 截断——Walker Walk pilot\n  expected_results:\n    eval_105K: 540\n    vs_baseline: -41%\n    nve_peak: 1.15\n    collapse: false\n    truncation_rate_at_dt2: 0.35\n    effective_horizon_mean: 11.2\n    issues:\n    - RSSM ensemble disagreement 校准不准——在 dt=1 transitions 上也频繁触发截断\n    - 有效 horizon 从 15 降至 ~11，减少了 long-range credit assignment\n    - 稳定但性能远低于 008e_v3 seed 1 (870) 和 baseline (916)\n  result_rationale: 'RSSM 本身不提供 well-calibrated uncertainty estimates（DreamerV3 使用\n    single RSSM， 不是 ensemble）。Pilot 需要额外实现 RSSM ensemble 或使用 KL divergence as proxy。\n    在 worst-tier 下，uncertainty estimate 噪声大：dt=1 transitions 的不确定性 也偶尔偏高（false truncation），而\n    dt>1 transitions 的不确定性不总是偏高 （missed truncation）。Net effect: truncation 防止了最严重的\n    collapse（NVE 不超 1.5x）， 但 over-truncation 缩短有效 horizon，损失 long-range learning signal。\n    Eval 540 好于 008d collapse (83) 但远低于 008e_v3 success (870)。 不适合作为 paper contribution——implementation\n    complexity 高但 benefit 有限。\n\n    '\n  tables: []\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: 'Uncertainty truncation 是 \"reasonable but noisy\" 的 mitigation。在 worst-tier\n    下 不足以写入论文——更适合 future work section 的 one-sentence mention。 CoRL deadline 前不值得投入更多\n    GPU。\n\n    '\n- name: Hopper Hop validation (3 seeds × 3 configs)\n  plan_id: plan_040\n  description: 第三 DMC locomotion 环境——worst-tier 预测：P2 优先级，可能不跑\n  expected_results:\n    likely_status: NOT RUN before CoRL deadline (P2 priority)\n    if_run:\n      baseline_mean: 250\n      trained_dt_emb_mean: 120\n      trained_dt_emb_nve_pattern: mixed — some seeds >1.0x, none >1.5x\n      no_dt_emb_mean: 130\n      separation: minimal\n  result_rationale: 'Hopper Hop 是 sparse reward + contact-rich dynamics，DreamerV3\n    baseline 仅 ~250 （远低于 Walker/Cheetah）。在 worst-tier 下，即使跑了，低 baseline 性能使得 v/e ratio\n    极不稳定（分母小），NVE 信噪比差，无法得出 clean 结论。 此外，45 GPU-hours 的预算在 13 天 deadline 前不值得投入——这些资源应用于\n    确保 Walker 数据的 presentation quality。\n\n    '\n  tables: []\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: 'P2 实验在 worst-tier 下应果断放弃。论文不需要第三个 negative result 来说明 CIVO 是 environment-specific。\n\n    '\n- name: Full cross-environment summary table\n  plan_id: N/A (synthesis)\n  description: 综合所有环境的 CIVO 检测结果\n  expected_results:\n    environments_with_confirmed_civo: 1\n    walker_walk:\n      civo_confirmed: true\n      nve_gt_1_5x_sensitivity: 3/3 (100%)\n      collapse_rate: 1/2 to 2/3 seeds\n      full_sgs_nve: 1.0\n      mechanism: observation-decoder-driven gradient amplification\n    cheetah_run:\n      civo_confirmed: false\n      nve_gt_1_5x_sensitivity: 0/3 (0%)\n      collapse_rate: 0/3\n      degradation: yes (-52% baseline)\n      mechanism: learning signal reduction + mild fidelity gap, no positive feedback\n        loop\n    cartpole_swingup:\n      civo_confirmed: false\n      nve_gt_1_5x_sensitivity: 0/3 (0%)\n      collapse_rate: 0/3\n      degradation: yes (-62% baseline)\n      mechanism: value suppression from sparse reward + dt>1 prediction noise\n    cross_env_threshold_accuracy: 0.65\n  result_rationale: 'Worst-tier 的 defining outcome：只有 Walker Walk 确认 CIVO。Cheetah\n    和 Cartpole 都显示 dt>1 degradation 但通过不同机制。1.5x NVE threshold 在 Walker 内完美 但跨环境仅\n    0.65 accuracy。这迫使论文完全退守 single-environment depth story。 贡献变为：(1) Walker Walk 的\n    rigorous factorial diagnosis，(2) NVE methodology （validated in Walker, proposed\n    with caveats），(3) gradient-level evidence （Full-SGS），(4) TAWM contrast（MPC vs\n    imagination）。 Drop 所有 \"general architectural vulnerability\" 语言。 Add extensive\n    limitations section 讨论 environment-specificity。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: Cross-environment CIVO summary\n    headers:\n    - Environment\n    - Degradation?\n    - CIVO (NVE>1.5x)?\n    - Collapse?\n    - Mechanism\n    rows:\n    - - Walker Walk\n      - Yes (-5% to -85%)\n      - Yes (3/3 seeds)\n      - Yes (1-2/3)\n      - CIVO + Pathway B\n    - - Cheetah Run\n      - Yes (-52%)\n      - No (0/3 seeds)\n      - No (0/3)\n      - Learning signal + fidelity gap\n    - - Cartpole Swingup\n      - Yes (-62%)\n      - No (0/3 seeds)\n      - No (0/3)\n      - Value suppression\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Cross-env NVE distribution violin plot: Walker (wide, right-skewed >1.5x) vs\n    Cheetah/Cartpole (narrow, centered <1.0x)'\n  analysis: '论文 framing 最终版： \"We provide the first rigorous factorial diagnosis of\n    why temporal abstraction fails in DreamerV3''s imagination-based training, demonstrated\n    in Walker Walk with controlled design. The CIVO mechanism — trained dt-embedding\n    amplifying RSSM fidelity gaps into value overestimation through observation decoder\n    gradients — is confirmed by gradient-level intervention (Full-SGS). Our NVE diagnostic\n    methodology achieves perfect separation in Walker Walk but does not generalize\n    to Cheetah Run or Cartpole Swingup, where degradation proceeds through different\n    mechanisms. This environment-specificity itself is an important finding: temporal\n    abstraction fails universally in our experiments, but the failure mode is environment-dependent,\n    complicating one-size-fits-all solutions. The contrast with TAWM (Nhu et al.,\n    ICML 2025), where dt-conditioning succeeds in MPC but fails in imagination, remains\n    the paper''s strongest novelty claim regardless of cross-environment generalization.\"'\n","numLines":1153,"startLine":1,"totalLines":1153}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_015f8tP9DPPryHJtwp4tA4th","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I've now read both the PDF paper and the review context YAML. Let me now dispatch the two reviewers in parallel, then conduct the full roundtable process.\n\nLet me understand the paper and context:\n\n**Paper**: \"Why Temporal Abstraction Fails in DreamerV3: A Single-Environment Diagnostic Analysis of Variable-Rate Imagination\"\n\n**Key claims**:\n1. Trained dt-embedding amplifies RSSM fidelity gaps → CIVO (conditioning-induced value overestimation)\n2. NVE diagnostic achieves perfect classification in Walker Walk (AUROC 0.98)\n\n\n3. CIVO appears environment-specific, failing to replicate in Cheetah and Cartpole\n4. Full-SGS eliminates CIVO entirely (NVE→1.00×)\n5. dt-conditioning succeeds in MPC but breaks down in imagination-based actor-critic\n\n**Review context (worst tier)**: The paper has narrowed to single-environment analysis. Cheetah and Cartpole show no CIVO signal, significantly limiting the scope of the contributions.\n\nNow I'm assigning two reviewers in parallel—R1 for methods and experiments, R2 for novelty and related work—then moving into the full roundtable discussion.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":40628,"cache_read_input_tokens":22971,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":40628},"output_tokens":19,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1b0edaaf-f3d3-4d02-90e4-a445b4dd87c2","uuid":"c28f5324-ea69-4789-b068-94b089f11e0e"}
