{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_015f8tP9DPPryHJtwp4tA4th","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Mibqf1WU3TJDQ7nWMwGzdf","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"R1: Methods + Experiments review","prompt":"You are Reviewer R1 for a top ML venue review (acceptance rate ~25%, 6-point scale: 1=Strong Reject, 6=Strong Accept). Your focus is **Methods and Experiments**.\n\n## Paper Summary\n\"Why Temporal Abstraction Fails in DreamerV3: A Single-Environment Diagnostic Analysis of Variable-Rate Imagination\"\n\nThe paper investigates why variable-rate imagination degrades performance in DreamerV3. It identifies a mechanism called CIVO (conditioning-induced value overestimation): a trained dt-embedding amplifies RSSM fidelity gaps through observation-decoder gradients, creating a positive feedback loop of value overestimation. The study is primarily conducted in Walker Walk, with negative cross-environment results in Cheetah Run and Cartpole Swingup.\n\n## Key Claims:\n1. Trained dt-embedding reliably triggers pathological overestimation (NVE>1.5×) in Walker Walk (3/3 seeds)\n2. Removing dt-embedding prevents CIVO (0/2 seeds exceed 1.5×)\n3. Frozen dt-embedding produces gradient starvation (distinct failure mode)\n4. NVE diagnostic achieves 5/5 accuracy in Walker Walk, AUROC 0.98\n5. Cross-environment: NVE diagnostic fails (accuracy 0.65, AUROC 0.72) — Cheetah and Cartpole degrade but without CIVO\n6. Full-SGS reduces NVE to 1.00×, proving observation-decoder-driven causation\n7. dt=1 imagination partially mitigates (1/4 seeds collapse via different \"Pathway B\" mechanism)\n8. Uncertainty-gated truncation pilot: prevents collapse but -41% performance (negative result)\n9. TAWM contrast: dt-conditioning works in MPC but fails in imagination-based AC\n\n## Experiment Design Reference (from review_context.yaml):\nThe full experiment plan includes these experiments. Check which are covered vs missing:\n\n**Walker Walk experiments (mostly covered):**\n- 008d (trained dt_emb, collapse) 3 seeds — COVERED in Table 1\n- 008f (dt_embed_dim=0) 2 seeds — COVERED in Table 2 (only 2 seeds, 1 killed)\n- 008e_v3 (dt=1 imag) 4 seeds — COVERED in Table 4\n- Frozen dt_emb — COVERED in Section 4.1.3\n- 008a (untrained dt_emb) 3 seeds — COVERED in Table 3\n- 008e_v3 additional seeds 3-4 — COVERED (4 seeds total in Table 4)\n- NVE threshold sensitivity — COVERED in Table 6 and Section 4.2\n- Full-SGS — COVERED in Section 4.5\n\n**Cheetah Run experiments:**\n- Baseline 3 seeds — mentioned but no detailed table\n- Trained dt_emb 3 seeds — COVERED in Table 7\n- dt_embed_dim=0 3 seeds — COVERED in Table 8\n- Untrained dt_emb + no subsample — mentioned briefly in text\n\n**Cartpole experiments:**\n- Baseline — mentioned but no table\n- Trained dt_emb — COVERED in Table 9\n- dt_embed_dim=0 — mentioned in text (eval 313, -1.3%)\n\n**Other analyses:**\n- RSSM fidelity — COVERED in Table 11\n- Actor entropy — COVERED in Section 4.4.2\n- Value distribution — COVERED in Section 4.4.3\n- dt-embedding cosine similarity — COVERED in Section 4.4.4\n- Uncertainty truncation pilot — COVERED in Section 4.6\n- Hopper Hop — NOT RUN (mentioned in plan as P2, likely dropped)\n\n**Key worst-case data from review context:**\n- Collapse rate in 008d is only 2/3 (50%), not deterministic\n- 008f seed 2 (009c) degrades to 148 (84% below baseline) — protection very unreliable\n- 008e_v3: 1/4 collapse, Pathway B closer to seed variance (with seeds 3-4 at 830/790)\n- Cheetah: 0/3 CIVO, trained vs no-dt-emb produces NO separation (407 vs 410)\n- Cartpole: 0/3 CIVO, also no separation (317 vs 313)\n- Cross-env NVE threshold accuracy only 0.65\n\n## Your Review Task (R1: Methods + Experiments)\n\nEvaluate:\n1. **Experimental methodology**: Is the factorial design sound? Are controls adequate?\n2. **Statistical rigor**: Are seed counts sufficient? Are claims appropriately hedged?\n3. **Metric validity**: Is NVE well-defined? Is the 1.5× threshold justified or post-hoc?\n4. **Experiment coverage**: Which planned experiments are missing or underreported?\n5. **Reproducibility**: Are enough details provided?\n6. **Internal consistency**: Do the results support the claims?\n7. **Negative results handling**: Are cross-environment failures reported honestly?\n\nProduce a structured review with:\n- Summary (2-3 sentences)\n- Strengths (bulleted)\n- Weaknesses (bulleted, with severity: major/minor)\n- Questions for Authors\n- Missing Experiments\n- Preliminary Score (1-6) with confidence (1-5)\n- Short justification for score\n\nBe rigorous but fair. This is a diagnostic/analysis paper, not a method paper proposing a solution."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":40628,"cache_read_input_tokens":22971,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":40628},"output_tokens":19,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1b0edaaf-f3d3-4d02-90e4-a445b4dd87c2","uuid":"b1ced972-32cb-4aac-8332-65bff7d9f35b"}
{"type":"system","subtype":"task_started","task_id":"a56f6209b607142a0","tool_use_id":"toolu_01Mibqf1WU3TJDQ7nWMwGzdf","description":"R1: Methods + Experiments review","task_type":"local_agent","prompt":"You are Reviewer R1 for a top ML venue review (acceptance rate ~25%, 6-point scale: 1=Strong Reject, 6=Strong Accept). Your focus is **Methods and Experiments**.\n\n## Paper Summary\n\"Why Temporal Abstraction Fails in DreamerV3: A Single-Environment Diagnostic Analysis of Variable-Rate Imagination\"\n\nThe paper investigates why variable-rate imagination degrades performance in DreamerV3. It identifies a mechanism called CIVO (conditioning-induced value overestimation): a trained dt-embedding amplifies RSSM fidelity gaps through observation-decoder gradients, creating a positive feedback loop of value overestimation. The study is primarily conducted in Walker Walk, with negative cross-environment results in Cheetah Run and Cartpole Swingup.\n\n## Key Claims:\n1. Trained dt-embedding reliably triggers pathological overestimation (NVE>1.5×) in Walker Walk (3/3 seeds)\n2. Removing dt-embedding prevents CIVO (0/2 seeds exceed 1.5×)\n3. Frozen dt-embedding produces gradient starvation (distinct failure mode)\n4. NVE diagnostic achieves 5/5 accuracy in Walker Walk, AUROC 0.98\n5. Cross-environment: NVE diagnostic fails (accuracy 0.65, AUROC 0.72) — Cheetah and Cartpole degrade but without CIVO\n6. Full-SGS reduces NVE to 1.00×, proving observation-decoder-driven causation\n7. dt=1 imagination partially mitigates (1/4 seeds collapse via different \"Pathway B\" mechanism)\n8. Uncertainty-gated truncation pilot: prevents collapse but -41% performance (negative result)\n9. TAWM contrast: dt-conditioning works in MPC but fails in imagination-based AC\n\n## Experiment Design Reference (from review_context.yaml):\nThe full experiment plan includes these experiments. Check which are covered vs missing:\n\n**Walker Walk experiments (mostly covered):**\n- 008d (trained dt_emb, collapse) 3 seeds — COVERED in Table 1\n- 008f (dt_embed_dim=0) 2 seeds — COVERED in Table 2 (only 2 seeds, 1 killed)\n- 008e_v3 (dt=1 imag) 4 seeds — COVERED in Table 4\n- Frozen dt_emb — COVERED in Section 4.1.3\n- 008a (untrained dt_emb) 3 seeds — COVERED in Table 3\n- 008e_v3 additional seeds 3-4 — COVERED (4 seeds total in Table 4)\n- NVE threshold sensitivity — COVERED in Table 6 and Section 4.2\n- Full-SGS — COVERED in Section 4.5\n\n**Cheetah Run experiments:**\n- Baseline 3 seeds — mentioned but no detailed table\n- Trained dt_emb 3 seeds — COVERED in Table 7\n- dt_embed_dim=0 3 seeds — COVERED in Table 8\n- Untrained dt_emb + no subsample — mentioned briefly in text\n\n**Cartpole experiments:**\n- Baseline — mentioned but no table\n- Trained dt_emb — COVERED in Table 9\n- dt_embed_dim=0 — mentioned in text (eval 313, -1.3%)\n\n**Other analyses:**\n- RSSM fidelity — COVERED in Table 11\n- Actor entropy — COVERED in Section 4.4.2\n- Value distribution — COVERED in Section 4.4.3\n- dt-embedding cosine similarity — COVERED in Section 4.4.4\n- Uncertainty truncation pilot — COVERED in Section 4.6\n- Hopper Hop — NOT RUN (mentioned in plan as P2, likely dropped)\n\n**Key worst-case data from review context:**\n- Collapse rate in 008d is only 2/3 (50%), not deterministic\n- 008f seed 2 (009c) degrades to 148 (84% below baseline) — protection very unreliable\n- 008e_v3: 1/4 collapse, Pathway B closer to seed variance (with seeds 3-4 at 830/790)\n- Cheetah: 0/3 CIVO, trained vs no-dt-emb produces NO separation (407 vs 410)\n- Cartpole: 0/3 CIVO, also no separation (317 vs 313)\n- Cross-env NVE threshold accuracy only 0.65\n\n## Your Review Task (R1: Methods + Experiments)\n\nEvaluate:\n1. **Experimental methodology**: Is the factorial design sound? Are controls adequate?\n2. **Statistical rigor**: Are seed counts sufficient? Are claims appropriately hedged?\n3. **Metric validity**: Is NVE well-defined? Is the 1.5× threshold justified or post-hoc?\n4. **Experiment coverage**: Which planned experiments are missing or underreported?\n5. **Reproducibility**: Are enough details provided?\n6. **Internal consistency**: Do the results support the claims?\n7. **Negative results handling**: Are cross-environment failures reported honestly?\n\nProduce a structured review with:\n- Summary (2-3 sentences)\n- Strengths (bulleted)\n- Weaknesses (bulleted, with severity: major/minor)\n- Questions for Authors\n- Missing Experiments\n- Preliminary Score (1-6) with confidence (1-5)\n- Short justification for score\n\nBe rigorous but fair. This is a diagnostic/analysis paper, not a method paper proposing a solution.","uuid":"e31a2f19-dfaa-4be1-b107-fcdea0cd8d01","session_id":"1b0edaaf-f3d3-4d02-90e4-a445b4dd87c2"}
