{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0173gwJ5p6NQ6cu1RcyHXs3H","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tTemporal abstraction via variable-rate imagination is a natural extension of world-model reinforcement learning, yet we find that every variable-rate configuration of DreamerV3 degrades performance---despite the success of identical $\\Delta t$-conditioning in MPC-based methods. Through a factorial diagnostic on Walker Walk, we identify the combination of trained temporal embedding and multi-rate data exposure as the causal factor and characterize the resulting failure mode: \\emph{conditioning-induced value overestimation} (CIVO). The trained embedding enables the RSSM reward head to develop a $2.78\\times$ prediction gap between $\\Delta t{=}1$ and $\\Delta t{=}2$, which the critic internalizes as optimistic values. Gradient decomposition shows that 93\\% of embedding gradients flow through observation decoders (0\\% from the reward head), establishing CIVO as observation-reconstruction-gradient-driven. Full-pathway gradient stopping (removing 93\\% of embedding gradients from observation decoders) completely eliminates CIVO, confirming the vulnerability is gradient-level. A normalized value-to-eval threshold of $1.5\\times$ (35K+ training window) achieves 7/8 classification ($n{=}8$, Walker Walk), with the single false positive arising from a mechanistically distinct non-CIVO collapse. The same CIVO trigger produces stochastic downstream outcomes across seeds---full collapse, transient CIVO with self-correction, and oscillatory degradation---from identical configurations. Critically, restricting imagination to $\\Delta t{=}1$ does not prevent collapse: one of two seeds fails via a distinct non-CIVO pathway with increasing entropy, revealing that trained temporal conditioning creates vulnerability through multiple mechanisms. Our analysis identifies the feedback architecture---imagination-based actor-critic bootstrapping versus MPC re-planning---as the structural factor that transforms manageable model imprecision into pathological value dynamics.\n2\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01TcjRwnpoLXHM9pNf7QHJEG","session_id":"1b0edaaf-f3d3-4d02-90e4-a445b4dd87c2","uuid":"e0bdf77b-5a3e-4ccb-a6a7-862235cee833","timestamp":"2026-05-16T14:27:40.341Z"}
