{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CiTkb1EiFV3YxWfjZtvfGG","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tnarrative_guidance: 'CIVO is a general architectural vulnerability in imagination-based\n2\t  actor-critic with dt-conditioning. Under best tier, the gradient decomposition (93%\n3\t  obs decoder → dt_emb, 7% KL, 0% reward) + Full-SGS (exp_018, NVE=1.00x→0.72x) closes\n4\t  the mechanism at gradient level. Cross-3-environment replication (Walker Walk ✓,\n5\t  Cheetah Run, PickCube/Cartpole) elevates the finding from DreamerV3-specific to\n6\t  structural warning for temporal-abstraction-in-world-models. TAWM contrast (MPC\n7\t  succeeds, imagination fails) is the headline novelty. The 1.5x NVE threshold maintains\n8\t  ≥3/4 separating power in every new environment. Pathway B (008e_v3_s2-type eval-driven\n9\t  collapse) is either rare (≤1/4 cross-env) or gets clean mechanistic characterization\n10\t  via control experiment. Missing from current plan: Full-SGS replication in Cheetah/Cartpole\n11\t  — needed to close \"gradient mechanism generalizes\" claim per tier spec.\n12\t\n13\t  '\n14\timagined_experiments:\n15\t- name: Walker Walk 008d (trained dt_emb, collapse) seeds 1-2\n16\t  plan_id: plan_011\n17\t  description: 'Replicate CIVO collapse with 2 additional seeds. Registry already\n18\t    has data: 009e (seed 1) collapsed NVE peak 4.12x; 009b (seed 2) self-corrected\n19\t    NVE peak 2.05x. Under best tier, both seeds exceed NVE>1.5x (confirmed), collapse\n20\t    is stochastic 1/2 (confirmed).\n21\t\n22\t    '\n23\t  expected_results:\n24\t    seed1_eval_105K: 131\n25\t    seed1_nve_peak: 4.12\n26\t    seed1_nve_peak_step: 55000\n27\t    seed1_collapse: true\n28\t    seed1_collapse_step: 55000\n29\t    seed2_eval_105K: 268\n30\t    seed2_nve_peak: 2.05\n31\t    seed2_nve_peak_step: 25000\n32\t    seed2_collapse: false\n33\t    seed2_self_correction_nve_105K: 0.38\n34\t    both_seeds_exceed_1.5x: true\n35\t    threshold_separating_power: 2/2 exceed 1.5x at 35K+\n36\t    collapse_rate: 1/2 (stochastic)\n37\t  result_rationale: 'Trained dt_emb creates systematic overestimation because the\n38\t    RSSM fidelity gap at dt=2 (obs gap 1.30x at inflated absolute levels, reward gap\n39\t    2.78x) is amplified through the observation decoder→dt_emb gradient pathway (93%\n40\t    of dt_emb gradient). Every seed with trained dt_emb reliably enters the pathological\n41\t    NVE>1.5x regime because the gradient mechanism is deterministic — the dt_emb learns\n42\t    to differentiate dt values, and the critic exploits this differentiation against\n43\t    inaccurate RSSM predictions. Whether NVE>1.5x becomes sustained (→collapse) or\n44\t    transient (→self-correction) depends on early training stochasticity: replay buffer\n45\t    sampling order, initialization, and whether the actor''s policy gradient from\n46\t    real returns can counteract the critic''s overestimate before it locks in (primacy\n47\t    bias, Qiao et al. 2023).\n48\t\n49\t    '\n50\t  tables:\n51\t  - name: NVE trajectory comparison (seed 1 vs seed 2)\n52\t    columns:\n53\t    - step\n54\t    - seed1_nve\n55\t    - seed1_eval\n56\t    - seed2_nve\n57\t    - seed2_eval\n58\t    rows:\n59\t    - - 25000\n60\t      - 1.78\n61\t      - 167\n62\t      - 2.05\n63\t      - 141\n64\t    - - 35000\n65\t      - 1.71\n66\t      - 146\n67\t      - 1.24\n68\t      - 164\n69\t    - - 45000\n70\t      - 2.09\n71\t      - 141\n72\t      - 1.62\n73\t      - 141\n74\t    - - 55000\n75\t      - 4.12\n76\t      - 83\n77\t      - 1.41\n78\t      - 172\n79\t    - - 65000\n80\t      - 1.23\n81\t      - 250\n82\t      - 0.94\n83\t      - 209\n84\t    - - 75000\n85\t      - 1.48\n86\t      - 178\n87\t      - 0.66\n88\t      - 197\n89\t    - - 85000\n90\t      - 1.15\n91\t      - 202\n92\t      - 0.51\n93\t      - 236\n94\t    - - 95000\n95\t      - 1.73\n96\t      - 133\n97\t      - 0.43\n98\t      - 279\n99\t    - - 105000\n100\t      - 1.57\n101\t      - 131\n102\t      - 0.38\n103\t      - 268\n104\t  figures_description:\n105\t  - 'NVE time series: seed 1 sustained >1.5x (35-55K) → collapse; seed 2 transient\n106\t    >1.5x (25-45K) → self-correction. Shaded 1.5x threshold line.'\n107\t  analysis: 'Actual data confirms best-tier predictions. 2/2 trained dt_emb seeds\n108\t    exceed NVE 1.5x, maintaining perfect threshold separating power (now 4/4 across\n109\t    trained/untrained combined). Collapse stochasticity (1/2) is a feature of the\n110\t    narrative: trained dt_emb is a necessary condition for CIVO, not sufficient for\n111\t    collapse. The sustained-vs-transient NVE persistence distinguishes the two outcomes.\n112\t\n113\t    '\n114\t- name: Walker Walk 008f (dt_embed_dim=0, stable) seeds 1-2\n115\t  plan_id: plan_012\n116\t  description: 'Replicate causal control stability. Seed 1 (009f) was killed (infra).\n117\t    Seed 2 (009c) ran to 105K: NVE peaked 1.26x, eval declined to 148. Under best\n118\t    tier, seed 1 re-run shows NVE<1.5x; seed 2 extended to 200K plateaus without crossing\n119\t    1.5x.\n120\t\n121\t    '\n122\t  expected_results:\n123\t    seed1_rerun_eval_105K: 420\n124\t    seed1_rerun_nve_peak: 0.95\n125\t    seed1_rerun_nve_105K: 0.35\n126\t    seed1_rerun_collapse: false\n127\t    seed2_eval_105K: 148\n128\t    seed2_nve_105K: 1.14\n129\t    seed2_eval_200K: 280\n130\t    seed2_nve_200K: 0.85\n131\t    seed2_nve_peak_ever: 1.26\n132\t    seed2_crosses_1.5x: false\n133\t    both_seeds_below_1.5x_at_35K_plus: true\n134\t    threshold_separating_power: 0/2 exceed 1.5x\n135\t  result_rationale: 'Without dt_embedding (dim=0), the critic receives no dt-conditioning\n136\t    information. The reward head cannot distinguish dt=1 from dt=2 transitions (reward\n137\t    gap 1.01x vs 2.78x with trained dt_emb), so the systematic overestimation feedback\n138\t    loop cannot form. Seed 2''s rising NVE at 105K (1.14x) reflects value inertia\n139\t    — value_mean was still rising (111.2@105K) while eval declined, but this is fundamentally\n140\t    different from CIVO: the value is simply slow to track a declining eval, not systematically\n141\t    overestimating. Extended to 200K, the value function adjusts downward as it accumulates\n142\t    more accurate return estimates, pulling NVE back below 1.0x. Seed 1 re-run (with\n143\t    stable infrastructure) follows the zigzag recovery pattern of 008f seed 0 (503@105K),\n144\t    because the underlying mechanism is the same — CIVO pathway is structurally blocked.\n145\t\n146\t    '\n147\t  tables:\n148\t  - name: Seed 2 extended trajectory (predicted 105K-200K)\n149\t    columns:\n150\t    - step"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01Mibqf1WU3TJDQ7nWMwGzdf","session_id":"1b0edaaf-f3d3-4d02-90e4-a445b4dd87c2","uuid":"11287c5e-6d05-43fb-b88a-530d41187a13","timestamp":"2026-05-16T14:27:50.895Z"}
