{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015exZHhZWCtCZmfoh6JK2LV","type":"tool_result","content":"150\t    - step\n151\t    - eval_return\n152\t    - nve\n153\t    - note\n154\t    rows:\n155\t    - - 105000\n156\t      - 148\n157\t      - 1.14\n158\t      - actual\n159\t    - - 125000\n160\t      - 195\n161\t      - 1.05\n162\t      - value still adjusting\n163\t    - - 145000\n164\t      - 240\n165\t      - 0.92\n166\t      - value correction begins\n167\t    - - 165000\n168\t      - 270\n169\t      - 0.88\n170\t      - eval recovering\n171\t    - - 185000\n172\t      - 290\n173\t      - 0.85\n174\t      - stabilizing\n175\t    - - 200000\n176\t      - 280\n177\t      - 0.85\n178\t      - plateau\n179\t  figures_description:\n180\t  - NVE trajectory for both seeds with 1.5x threshold line. Demonstrates NVE never\n181\t    crosses 1.5x, contrasting with 008d seeds.\n182\t  analysis: 'Seed 2''s decline after 75K is concerning but does NOT constitute CIVO\n183\t    — NVE never exceeded 1.5x, and the value dynamics are qualitatively different\n184\t    (slow value tracking vs value explosion). The 200K extension confirms plateau\n185\t    without threshold crossing. Seed 1 re-run expected to show healthier zigzag recovery\n186\t    (like seed 0), improving cross-seed consistency. Critical for C2: 0/2 untrained\n187\t    seeds cross 1.5x, maintaining 4/4→6/6 threshold separation when combined with\n188\t    plan_011.\n189\t\n190\t    '\n191\t- name: Walker Walk 008e_v3 (mitigation) seeds 1-2\n192\t  plan_id: plan_014\n193\t  description: 'Multi-seed validation of dt=1 imagination mitigation. Already done:\n194\t    seed 1 success (869.9@105K), seed 2 collapsed (137@105K) via non-CIVO Pathway\n195\t    B. Under best tier, Pathway B gets clean mechanistic characterization.\n196\t\n197\t    '\n198\t  expected_results:\n199\t    seed1_eval_105K: 869.9\n200\t    seed1_nve_105K: 0.8\n201\t    seed1_collapse: false\n202\t    seed2_eval_105K: 137\n203\t    seed2_nve_105K: 3.78\n204\t    seed2_collapse: true\n205\t    seed2_pathway: B (eval-driven, entropy↑)\n206\t    seed2_actor_entropy_collapse: -5.21_to_-3.83\n207\t    pathway_b_rate_walker: 1/2\n208\t    pathway_a_blocked: true\n209\t    gate_dt_mean_both_seeds: 1.0\n210\t  result_rationale: 'dt=1 imagination blocks Pathway A (classic CIVO) because the\n211\t    critic never evaluates dt>1 imagination steps — the value overestimation feedback\n212\t    loop requires dt>1 predictions where RSSM fidelity degrades. However, the trained\n213\t    dt_embedding still receives gradient from observation decoders during world model\n214\t    training on real dt>1 transitions (subsample ON includes dt=2 in training data).\n215\t    This creates a secondary vulnerability: the dt_emb encodes dt-specific information\n216\t    that subtly corrupts the latent state representation, even when imagination uses\n217\t    only dt=1. Seed 2''s collapse shows eval-driven destabilization (715→452→137)\n218\t    with increasing entropy (-5.21→-3.83), the opposite signature of CIVO (which has\n219\t    decreasing entropy). The policy destabilizes because the world model''s latent\n220\t    space has been distorted by the trained dt_emb, not because the critic directly\n221\t    overestimates. This Pathway B is stochastic — seed 1 avoids it because its specific\n222\t    initialization leads to a latent representation that is less corrupted by the\n223\t    dt_emb gradients.\n224\t\n225\t    '\n226\t  tables:\n227\t  - name: Pathway A vs Pathway B signature comparison\n228\t    columns:\n229\t    - feature\n230\t    - pathway_a_008d_s1\n231\t    - pathway_b_008e_v3_s2\n232\t    rows:\n233\t    - - value change at collapse\n234\t      - +130% explosion\n235\t      - +13% mild\n236\t    - - eval change at collapse\n237\t      - -43% follows value\n238\t      - -81% leads\n239\t    - - NVE driver\n240\t      - value numerator\n241\t      - eval denominator\n242\t    - - actor_entropy\n243\t      - ↓ (-3.47→-4.88) deterministic\n244\t      - ↑ (-5.21→-3.83) random\n245\t    - - mechanism\n246\t      - critic overestimate → actor exploit\n247\t      - eval crash → value lag\n248\t  figures_description:\n249\t  - 'Dual-panel: seed 1 healthy trajectory vs seed 2 Pathway B collapse, with entropy\n250\t    overlay showing opposite signatures.'\n251\t  analysis: 'C6 is partially falsified but transformed into a stronger finding: trained\n252\t    dt_embedding creates vulnerability through MULTIPLE pathways. dt=1 imagination\n253\t    eliminates the more understood Pathway A but exposes the previously hidden Pathway\n254\t    B. Under best tier, Pathway B is characterized cleanly enough that it becomes\n255\t    a contribution rather than a weakness — the paper demonstrates that surface-level\n256\t    mitigations are insufficient.\n257\t\n258\t    '\n259\t- name: Walker Walk 008a (untrained dt_emb, V-recovery) seeds 1-2\n260\t  plan_id: plan_013\n261\t  description: 'Replicate value growth suppression and V-recovery pattern with 2 additional\n262\t    seeds. Seed 0 showed 778@105K (85% baseline), NVE=0.59x with two dip-recovery\n263\t    cycles.\n264\t\n265\t    '\n266\t  expected_results:\n267\t    seed1_eval_105K: 720\n268\t    seed1_nve_range:\n269\t    - 0.55\n270\t    - 0.9\n271\t    seed1_nve_105K: 0.62\n272\t    seed1_v_recovery_count: 2\n273\t    seed1_collapse: false\n274\t    seed2_eval_105K: 690\n275\t    seed2_nve_range:\n276\t    - 0.5\n277\t    - 0.95\n278\t    seed2_nve_105K: 0.58\n279\t    seed2_v_recovery_count: 1\n280\t    seed2_collapse: false\n281\t    cross_seed_mean_eval_105K: 729\n282\t    cross_seed_mean_nve_105K: 0.6\n283\t    vs_baseline_105K: -20% (range -15% to -25%)\n284\t  result_rationale: 'Untrained dt_emb (subsample OFF, so dt_emb trains but never sees\n285\t    dt>1 data) means the embedding learns from dt=1 transitions only. When imagination\n286\t    encounters dt>1 predictions, the dt_emb provides random-equivalent conditioning\n287\t    for those values. The critic cannot form dt-specific overestimates because the\n288\t    dt_emb carries no learned dt>1 information. NVE stays structurally suppressed\n289\t    (0.5-0.9x) because value growth is bounded by the quality of dt=1-only imagination.\n290\t    The V-recovery pattern (zigzag) arises from periodic exploration-exploitation\n291\t    oscillation in a regime where the critic is conservative. New seeds show similar\n292\t    pattern with ±10% variance in eval (driven by early exploration stochasticity),\n293\t    but the NVE suppression is robust because it''s a structural property of the unexposed\n294\t    dt_emb, not a stochastic outcome.\n295\t\n296\t    '\n297\t  tables:\n298\t  - name: Cross-seed V-recovery summary\n299\t    columns:\n300\t    - seed\n301\t    - eval_55K\n302\t    - eval_65K\n303\t    - eval_85K\n304\t    - eval_105K\n305\t    - nve_55K\n306\t    - nve_105K\n307\t    rows:\n308\t    - - 0\n309\t      - 488\n310\t      - 608\n311\t      - 584\n312\t      - 778\n313\t      - 0.93\n314\t      - 0.59\n315\t    - - 1\n316\t      - 450\n317\t      - 570\n318\t      - 620\n319\t      - 720\n320\t      - 0.85\n321\t      - 0.62\n322\t    - - 2\n323\t      - 420\n324\t      - 540\n325\t      - 560\n326\t      - 690\n327\t      - 0.9\n328\t      - 0.58\n329\t  figures_description:\n330\t  - 3-seed learning curves with confidence bands, showing V-recovery pattern reproducibility.\n331\t    NVE overlay stays below 1.0x throughout.\n332\t  analysis: 'Confirms C3 robustly: untrained dt_emb provides structural protection.\n333\t    The ±10% eval variance across seeds is well within DreamerV3''s typical seed variability.\n334\t    The key invariant — NVE never exceeds 1.0x at 35K+ — holds across all seeds, consistent\n335\t    with the gradient-level explanation (dt_emb unexposed to dt>1 data → no dt>1-specific\n336\t    gradient signal → no systematic overestimation).\n337\t\n338\t    '\n339\t- name: Walker Walk FROZEN dt_emb + subsample ON + dt=2 imag + H=8\n340\t  plan_id: plan_015\n341\t  description: 'Already run as exp_015b. NVE 0.39-0.47 (far below 1.0), actor_loss→0\n342\t    (gradient starvation), eval volatile 80-238. Under best tier, this confirms dt_emb\n343\t    TRAINING is the necessary condition for CIVO, with frozen dt_emb revealing a distinct\n344\t    failure mode (gradient starvation ≠ CIVO).\n345\t\n346\t    '\n347\t  expected_results:\n348\t    eval_105K: 204\n349\t    nve_range:"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01Mibqf1WU3TJDQ7nWMwGzdf","session_id":"1b0edaaf-f3d3-4d02-90e4-a445b4dd87c2","uuid":"7ef03ed7-12c9-4fb1-bede-b98773bfd263","timestamp":"2026-05-16T14:27:54.422Z"}
