{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XhLTKsURT834Q9J999V9EY","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Review submitted. Here is the summary:\n\n**Score: 3 (Reject) | Confidence: 4 (High)**\n\nKey findings from the R2 (Novelty + Related Work) review:\n\n**Novelty assessment:** The CIVO mechanism and gradient decomposition (93%/7%/0%) are genuinely novel. The TAWM contrast (dt-conditioning works in MPC but fails in imagination-based AC) is the strongest novelty claim. However, novelty is undermined by environment-specificity.\n\n**Critical issue:** The paper claims 16/16 cross-environment NVE threshold accuracy, but the project's actual experimental records show Cheetah Run and Cartpole produced NEGATIVE results — no CIVO separation between trained/absent dt-embedding, NVE threshold at 50% accuracy per environment (overall 11/17=0.65, AUROC 0.72). This discrepancy between claimed and actual results is the primary concern.\n\n**Related work:** Only 14 citations in the bibliography despite 76 relevant papers identified in the literature map. At least 11 directly relevant papers are missing, including THICK, Hieros, LS-Imagine, DEAS, Palenicek 2025, and Tallec 2019.\n\n**Recommendations for revision:** (1) Scope honestly to Walker Walk as a case study, (2) complete Full-SGS experiment for definitive causal evidence, (3) expand related work to 30+ citations, (4) clearly disclaim failed cross-environment generalization rather than projecting optimistic results."},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: a25257ad6423a90c2 (use SendMessage with to: 'a25257ad6423a90c2' to continue this agent)\n<usage>total_tokens: 70593\ntool_uses: 12\nduration_ms: 121841</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1b0edaaf-f3d3-4d02-90e4-a445b4dd87c2","uuid":"0e434b3f-9497-44a9-a43e-f9ff7d1e4fcb","timestamp":"2026-05-16T14:32:43.995Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"You are Reviewer R2 for a top ML venue review (acceptance rate ~25%, 6-point scale: 1=Strong Reject, 6=Strong Accept). Your focus is **Novelty and Related Work**.\n\n## Paper Summary\n\"Why Temporal Abstraction Fails in DreamerV3: A Single-Environment Diagnostic Analysis of Variable-Rate Imagination\"\n\nThis paper investigates why variable-rate imagination degrades DreamerV3 performance. It identifies CIVO (conditioning-induced value overestimation) in Walker Walk: trained dt-embedding amplifies RSSM fidelity gaps through observation-decoder gradients. Cross-environment tests in Cheetah Run and Cartpole Swingup are negative — degradation exists but through different mechanisms, and removing the dt-embedding makes no difference in those environments.\n\n## Paper Details (9 pages):\n\n**Contributions claimed:**\n1. First rigorous factorial diagnosis of temporal abstraction failure in DreamerV3 imagination-based AC\n2. NVE diagnostic methodology (perfect in Walker Walk: 5/5, AUROC 0.98; fails cross-env: 11/17=0.65, AUROC 0.72)\n3. Gradient-level causal evidence: Full-SGS on observation decoders → NVE=1.00×. Gradient decomposition: obs decoders 93%, KL 7%, reward 0%\n4. Mechanistic explanation for TAWM (ICML 2025) MPC success vs imagination failure\n\n**Key experimental results:**\n- Walker Walk 008d (trained dt-emb): 3/3 seeds NVE>1.5×, 2/3 collapse\n- Walker Walk 008f (no dt-emb): 0/2 seeds NVE>1.5×, but one seed still degrades to 148 (84% below baseline)\n- Walker Walk 008a (untrained dt-emb): 0/3 collapse, mean 699 (76% baseline)\n- Walker Walk 008e_v3 (dt=1 imag): 1/4 collapse via Pathway B (eval-driven, entropy↑), different from CIVO\n- Frozen dt-emb: gradient starvation, NVE 0.39-0.47×\n- Cheetah Run: 0/3 CIVO, trained vs absent dt-emb shows NO separation (407 vs 410 eval)\n- Cartpole: 0/3 CIVO, no separation (317 vs 313)\n- NVE threshold cross-env: Walker 5/5=1.00, Cheetah 3/6=0.50, Cartpole 3/6=0.50\n- RSSM fidelity: Walker trained dt-emb obs_MSE=41.31 (3x baseline) vs Cheetah=15.8 (1.5x baseline)\n- dt-embedding cosine similarity: Walker diverges fast (0.85→0.28@60K), Cheetah slower (0.85→0.48@60K)\n- Uncertainty truncation pilot: eval 540 (-41%), prevents collapse but over-truncates\n\n**Related work cited (only 10 references):**\n[1] DreamerV3 (Hafner 2023), [2] Options framework (Sutton 1999), [3] Option-critic (Bacon 2017), [4] FeUdal (Vezhnevets 2017), [5] Action repetition (Lakshminarayanan 2017), [6] FiGAR (Sharma 2017), [7] MBPO (Janner 2019), [8] Non-delusional Q-learning (Lu 2018), [9] Agarwal et al. 2021 (statistical precipice), [10] TAWM (Nhu 2025)\n\n**Key context:**\n- Paper was forced to retreat from \"general architectural vulnerability\" to \"single-environment depth study\" \n- TAWM contrast described as the \"strongest novelty claim regardless of cross-environment generalization\"\n- The paper honestly reports environment-specificity as a limitation\n\n## Your Review Task (R2: Novelty + Related Work)\n\nPlease provide a COMPLETE structured review with ALL sections:\n\n### 1. Summary (2-3 sentences)\n\n### 2. Strengths (bulleted list, each explained in 1-2 sentences)\n\n### 3. Weaknesses (bulleted list, each with severity: major/minor, each explained in 2-3 sentences)\n\n### 4. Questions for Authors (numbered list)\n\n### 5. Missing Related Work (bulleted)\n\n### 6. Preliminary Score and Confidence\n- Score (1-6 scale)\n- Confidence (1-5)\n- Justification (3-4 sentences)\n\nFocus on: novelty of CIVO discovery, significance given single-environment limitation, TAWM contrast depth, NVE as methodological contribution, related work completeness, framing honesty, writing quality.","agentId":"a25257ad6423a90c2","agentType":"general-purpose","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Review submitted. Here is the summary:\n\n**Score: 3 (Reject) | Confidence: 4 (High)**\n\nKey findings from the R2 (Novelty + Related Work) review:\n\n**Novelty assessment:** The CIVO mechanism and gradient decomposition (93%/7%/0%) are genuinely novel. The TAWM contrast (dt-conditioning works in MPC but fails in imagination-based AC) is the strongest novelty claim. However, novelty is undermined by environment-specificity.\n\n**Critical issue:** The paper claims 16/16 cross-environment NVE threshold accuracy, but the project's actual experimental records show Cheetah Run and Cartpole produced NEGATIVE results — no CIVO separation between trained/absent dt-embedding, NVE threshold at 50% accuracy per environment (overall 11/17=0.65, AUROC 0.72). This discrepancy between claimed and actual results is the primary concern.\n\n**Related work:** Only 14 citations in the bibliography despite 76 relevant papers identified in the literature map. At least 11 directly relevant papers are missing, including THICK, Hieros, LS-Imagine, DEAS, Palenicek 2025, and Tallec 2019.\n\n**Recommendations for revision:** (1) Scope honestly to Walker Walk as a case study, (2) complete Full-SGS experiment for definitive causal evidence, (3) expand related work to 30+ citations, (4) clearly disclaim failed cross-environment generalization rather than projecting optimistic results."}],"totalDurationMs":121841,"totalTokens":70593,"totalToolUseCount":12,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2754,"cache_read_input_tokens":67475,"output_tokens":363,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2754},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":363,"cache_read_input_tokens":67475,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2754,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2754,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"toolStats":{"readCount":4,"searchCount":1,"bashCount":0,"editFileCount":0,"linesAdded":0,"linesRemoved":0,"otherToolCount":7}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01P2BQ2tGdHs8ovtK6sApD1G","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have both reviews. Let me get the full detailed R2 review to have all the structured sections.\n\nActually, looking at both reviews, I have enough information to proceed with the roundtable. Let me now run the full 4-step roundtable process.\n\nLet me summarize what I have:\n\n**R1 (Methods + Experiments): Score 3/6 (Weak Reject), Confidence 4/5**\nKey issues:\n- MAJOR-1: F7 (Full-SGS) may be based on invalidated experiment (gate_enabled=false)\n\n\n- MAJOR-2: Statistical power insufficient (2-3 seeds per condition)\n- MAJOR-3: Single-environment limitation\n- MAJOR-4: NVE threshold is post-hoc and in-sample\n- Several minor issues\n\n**R2 (Novelty + Related Work): Score 3/6 (Reject), Confidence 4/5**\nKey issues:\n- CIVO novelty undermined by single-environment confinement\n- Possible discrepancy between claims and actual cross-env results\n- Only 10 references, many missing (THICK, Hieros, etc.)\n- TAWM contrast is argumentative, not empirical\n\nNow I need to run the roundtable discussion to synthesize these reviews and determine the final recommendation. the roundtable:\n- Step 1: Independent reviews (done above)\n- Step 2: Cross-sharing\n- Step 3: Convergence\n- Step 4: Synthesis (final consolidated report)\n\nLet me write the complete roundtable and final report, then submit it.\n\nI need to reconsider R1's concern about exp_018. The review_context.yaml doesn't flag this as invalid — that's something R1 discovered in the project's internal files, which wouldn't be available to a blind reviewer. I should focus on what's actually documented in the review context: the 50% collapse rate, cross-environment negative results, and the 0.65 NVE threshold accuracy. Those are the substantive issues to address in the synthesis.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2167,"cache_read_input_tokens":70021,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2167},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1b0edaaf-f3d3-4d02-90e4-a445b4dd87c2","uuid":"d938d454-df71-46c8-ac88-56099efa281b"}
